{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-wasm.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:35:23.251071Z","id":"7e91434f9bd90b956ab7c5a17a3dc20736797b9733de4fad82e796ac55075b46","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"No longer true: scripts/quality_gates.sh:158 runs scripts/check-wasm.sh (the thread's close, cc73bc73), and the script now also checks clax-content-git (scripts/check-wasm.sh:2-4).","supersedes":"f7a7babd97c31991fc6c0cffaff7a09bd20a7883e38d1a84d0622e6c162e102d","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-clients.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:23.153271Z","id":"d5bf7790d56e2ef77e9188e4f838271a7fa7c2df25d43e72e2f571340e7ea94a","body":{"detail":"The measure is the median, over slow_rounds floods of flood_batches document batches, of the daemon's footprint growth (budget 1024 KB). Measured medians were 0-32 KB per flood with and without CPU load, against 320-448 KB for the earlier single-flood RSS measure. A build that keeps a slow client's whole backlog (QUEUE in crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs raised from 64 to 1<<20) was built but never measured: its first run stalled in macOS's assessment of new executables. That a kept backlog exceeds the budget is inferred from its size (5000 events with 160-character paths per flood), not observed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":827},"end":{"line":837},"content_hash":"be67e806b167263d6cedfacadd444a8750ddaa218457c63c4f32d442b666ac9e"},"suggested_fix":"Run scripts/perf-clients.py --quick once against that variant binary and confirm slow_growth_kb fails.","summary":"slow_growth_kb has not been shown to catch a kept backlog","supersedes":"2fae41b92c5d2a7666d11c3a6fb18f6e96b7466d6d9f7db468f0e8e22cfe2922","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/npm-ci-stamped.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:21:31.835008Z","id":"1bbd149ecbccd48cd976630f7121239641fe9b92fd8daef0106c6198c35cba74","body":{"detail":"web/ and plugins/pi/ moved to pnpm (scripts/pnpm-install-stamped.sh, pnpm-lock.yaml); crates/clax-worker kept npm and its package-lock.json, so this stamped npm ci stays for it alone (scripts/quality_gates.sh lane_worker, just worker-test). Moving it means a pnpm-lock.yaml for wrangler and its workerd and esbuild install scripts, which pnpm runs only when allowBuilds lists them (web/pnpm-workspace.yaml allows none), and an unchanged deploy path for crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs and scripts/cloudflare-setup.sh, which run npm.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2},"end":{"line":3},"content_hash":"678ec3cbf9e49427879ba05b2fcb42a99778769e4fe186058dabbab2aa3ac421"},"summary":"crates/clax-worker installs with pnpm, as web/ and plugins/pi/ do","tags":["build","revisit:the Worker's packages come under Bazel, or npm leaves the machines that run the gates","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-wasm.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:35.311207Z","id":"93e0f83d91a850717ad4f58f21482ec4ec4b9bbc14fdb94652f95d2c10285326","body":{"detail":".github/workflows/ci.yml and rust-toolchain.toml add the wasm32-unknown-unknown target, and the script now also tries Debian and Ubuntu's /usr/lib/llvm-<N>/bin. Whether ubuntu-latest has a clang there that targets wasm32 beside an llvm-ar was not checked; the first CI run of the gates shows it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":30},"end":{"line":42},"content_hash":"e66b7d02889242a086cff19ef6e715715aeb07f55cc86dd9f77faecf1ca7e1c7"},"summary":"The wasm32 lane has run on macOS only: CI's Ubuntu LLVM is unverified","supersedes":"66e95d2ea22782cbc37390be298fd766ce5ef445f0e65031e13510713967d590","tags":["gates","ci","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:35.341823Z","id":"69fa4332dd9c3d30ee14a84f1597e6546f828db881567aabbc837c3938bfbdd7","body":{"detail":"They run first, alone, because several were timing-sensitive. Since 5da6c9a the view-mounting and child-process tests run under limits that end hangs only (MOUNT_TIMEOUT_MS 30 s, CHILD_TIMEOUT_MS 60 s, web/shell/src/test/timeouts.ts), so moving them into the lanes would save about 9 s of a gates run.","kind":"suggestion","ref":"git:e01d4166","span":{"start":{"line":162},"end":{"line":168},"content_hash":"82fe20109f02bee76696788391627a4839b255388a7a3efecad0187f317922f8"},"summary":"The shell's unit tests run alone (about 9 s); they may now join the lanes","supersedes":"0256afa979a18b3e310fc022b681eab3bb8d4f5157de3ae88f505bef6746877c","tags":["gate-speed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-crate-layers.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:52:20.537149Z","id":"904f8fe2617a660a7b40d8ce6a99608d286b2a72ba8c9ba0409327bf9486ffff","body":{"detail":"The layout's picture (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-workspace-layout-design.md section 2.1, lines 184-188) and ALLOWED here gain the crates the hosted work added: clax-rt (the runtime seam, tokio natively and a Worker's event loop on wasm32) depends on no workspace crate and every daemon crate uses it, so it joins clax-core's set; clax-git depends on nothing; clax-content-git on clax-core, clax-rt and clax-git. crates/clax-worker stays outside the workspace. This amends the decided layout spec, which is the owner's.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":31},"end":{"line":48},"content_hash":"8239201ac2a10212769d2e0e165229b85b50b75ec65a63159416546a23401147"},"summary":"Place clax-rt beside clax-core, clax-git on its own and clax-content-git over both in the layout","tags":["layout","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-clients.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:55:11.514108Z","id":"cede54937cd346ae19c60a8ab7e67c824d62cb677f6b17313455613849061ff3","body":{"detail":"The measure is the median, over slow_rounds floods of flood_batches document batches, of the daemon's footprint growth (budget 1024 KB). Measured medians were 0-32 KB per flood with and without CPU load, against 320-448 KB for the earlier single-flood RSS measure. A build that keeps a slow client's whole backlog (QUEUE in crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs raised from 64 to 1<<20) was built but never measured: its first run stalled in macOS's assessment of new executables. That a kept backlog exceeds the budget is inferred from its size (5000 events with 160-character paths per flood), not observed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":829},"end":{"line":839},"content_hash":"be67e806b167263d6cedfacadd444a8750ddaa218457c63c4f32d442b666ac9e"},"suggested_fix":"Run scripts/perf-clients.py --quick once against that variant binary and confirm slow_growth_kb fails.","summary":"slow_growth_kb has not been shown to catch a kept backlog","supersedes":"d5bf7790d56e2ef77e9188e4f838271a7fa7c2df25d43e72e2f571340e7ea94a","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:55:11.546191Z","id":"19ed076eac262bec12a035436c05705e62de550b5728608bfe916336fa552b44","body":{"detail":"test-repos.mjs needs jj (CLAX_TEST_JJ or jj on PATH) and fails without it; no gate installs one. After commit cfe9fdaa it passes with CLAX_TEST_JJ set (node test-repos.mjs --no-build: every check ok). The e2e lane's node e2e.mjs now publishes into git through the stand-in (REPO_STORE=memory) but does not clone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":140},"end":{"line":147},"content_hash":"b307cd78ca40244b0f066e84429c5be8f1d9fc44367795b203ac88b7d8c11c78"},"summary":"The worker lane does not run crates/clax-worker/test-repos.mjs (the RepoDO stand-in, /git/ clones and pushes, R2 assets)","supersedes":"b186353e057e2a4c353cbab7a1da788a980a4c83430c17d1f2d2dcb722ea6f3b","tags":["worker","gates","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/crate-package.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T03:22:35.072654Z","id":"54f2cebff7455dc8dd70dfaefffba283d87f7ff21b1166c392264ac987cb2e35","body":{"detail":"Not taken: it makes about eleven internal crates (clax-core, clax-store, clax-server, ...) public crates.io names that others can depend on, each release has to publish them in layer order with versioned path dependencies, and clax-embedded would still need its web UI, extension and plugins copied inside its own directory at publish time. The generated package keeps every internal crate private at the cost of rewriting paths (rewrite_sources, lines 211-232).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2},"end":{"line":38},"content_hash":"853c6518c8dbe0dbd3c800cd1bed9b5cb258f83c6d6ddd0c64245866ec5564fe"},"summary":"Publish every workspace crate to crates.io instead of one generated clax package","tags":["revisit:a workspace crate is wanted as a library on crates.io, or the path rewrite in scripts/crate-package.py breaks on a source pattern it cannot handle","session:claude-code:b2fe0abc-990b-4628-b4c7-4c6d7f3f261b"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/crate-package.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T03:22:35.110063Z","id":"24303270533236998727e5f7ca681eed8273d90551f9ca9be3237987f3c06117","body":{"detail":"rewrite_sources replaces every crate:: in a bundled library crate's sources with crate::<module>:: and every clax_<name>:: with crate::clax_<name>::, comments and string literals included. True of the sources at this commit (git grep finds none of these patterns in the eleven bundled crates' src/). A #[macro_export] macro would move to the package root and break its crate::<module>:: callers; a crate feature would be dropped (merged_dependencies refuses optional dependencies); a string such as a serde 'with = \"crate::x\"' is rewritten, which is right, but a log or error message quoting a path would change. tracing targets already read clax::clax_server::... in the package instead of clax_server::... . just crate-package (cargo check --locked of the packed crate) catches whatever does not compile.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":211},"end":{"line":232},"content_hash":"10cea40f7e1f818dfdb6c107a712446c3b8fb861b56b0d468eb7956b1cdb7ce0"},"summary":"The package's module rewrite is textual and assumes the bundled crates have no #[macro_export] macros, no extern crate, no crate features and no strings naming crate paths","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fe0abc-990b-4628-b4c7-4c6d7f3f261b"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:43:16.231572Z","id":"68efba6f9058766e3913758d626735c91e5cc05725d36bfc013a89029fdf4082","body":{"detail":"scripts/test-build-app-clax.sh checks scripts/build-app-clax.sh (the dry-run commands per platform and profile, and that place renames a binary into place rather than writing over it) in about a second, with no build. lane_scripts does not run it yet; add: run \"build app clax\" bash scripts/test-build-app-clax.sh","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":69},"end":{"line":75},"content_hash":"6cc1e1256a06c75d99f717cf75587dae4d3d430d62666bff5748f1b81bb179c4"},"suggested_fix":"Append `&& run \"build app clax\" scripts/test-build-app-clax.sh` to lane_scripts.","summary":"Add scripts/test-build-app-clax.sh to lane_scripts","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-clax.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:43:16.267329Z","id":"87888a6c851e5ee5685c4f01036464e501fb2d73299c977a5885e25f3de84ec2","body":{"detail":"build-app-clax.sh reads the NDK's linkers and llvm-strip from toolchains/llvm/prebuilt/darwin-x86_64/bin. On a Linux host (for example a CI runner) that directory is linux-x86_64, so the Android build fails there. macOS is the only host the app builds on today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"09b850f06c7cae12eeb8058727664f29cd3347bb06c6bdd77065659f4c45838e"},"suggested_fix":"Pick the prebuilt directory from `uname -s` (darwin-x86_64 or linux-x86_64) when a Linux host needs it.","summary":"The NDK toolchain path assumes a macOS host","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-clax.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:01:02.549258Z","id":"688a1a4ebb8462d93bf00159a978838a27eef14d5b16f26e7a891a1ed0598577","body":{"detail":"With --debug, cargo builds without --release, and crates/clax-server/src/routes/shell.rs:13-15 derives RustEmbed for ../../web/dist/ without rust-embed's debug-embed feature (Cargo.toml:35), so a debug binary reads web/dist from the build machine's checkout at run time instead of embedding it. Placed as jniLibs/<abi>/libclax.so by 'scripts/build-app-clax.sh android --debug', it runs on the device but every shell route finds no files. The script's header (lines 2-11) does not say this. A macOS --debug build works only while the checkout stays in place.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":37},"end":{"line":38},"content_hash":"9f90582cc8690f00ee4c05ffaf3820af8cc6e3cb2716f754e9ff450d083c9be4"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse --debug for android (or all), or say in the header and usage that a --debug build is host-only and not self-contained.","summary":"A --debug build places a clax that serves no web UI on Android","tags":["reviewer","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:31:23.489166Z","id":"8dd768000034ae1b91ce3a0ac053106ba7d4999efdbfdea1da3ae259ee28b945","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:49a0cccabd27","summary":"lane_scripts in scripts/quality_gates.sh now runs: run \"build app clax\" bash scripts/test-build-app-clax.sh. bash scripts/test-build-app-clax.sh prints only PASS lines and exits 0; bash -n scripts/quality_gates.sh passes.","supersedes":"68efba6f9058766e3913758d626735c91e5cc05725d36bfc013a89029fdf4082","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:09:51.141793Z","id":"c5a83fb64fbbfd0d4ff2428d1ee5394b149c6da386b6eb8f404148cb60e34ab5","body":{"detail":"They run first, alone, because several were timing-sensitive. Since 5da6c9a4430e the view-mounting and child-process tests run under limits that end hangs only (MOUNT_TIMEOUT_MS 30 s, CHILD_TIMEOUT_MS 60 s, web/shell/src/test/timeouts.ts), so moving them into the lanes would save about 9 s of a gates run.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":153},"end":{"line":159},"content_hash":"43ba07359a2927073b8825eff55b3404c52ce0a02a6b7953d444a1c18c2256c6"},"summary":"The shell's unit tests run alone (about 9 s); they may now join the lanes","supersedes":"39562e1125375035c0a8ea3214e707f7ee268df5e36d450a5c361549026fe126","tags":["gate-speed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-home-bundle.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:54:52.511668Z","id":"a58f4ba9d767c7e1ec9f1a6b575b672ae20c1443b3aa8d62cab5eedb8918d3d0","body":{"detail":"Why this key: lib/bundle/trust.dart decide() matches an installed app to a bundle by lineage AND author key, so every shipped release must carry the same key or installs treat it as a foreign lineage (no silent update, spec 2026-10-16-home-screen-app-design §5). A key committed to the repository would let anyone sign a bundle on the home lineage that installs accept as an update of the home app, which holds the home capability; this install's own BundleKey (lib/platform/bundle_key.dart) differs per device, so it cannot sign a shared release. The public key is recorded in apps/clax_app/assets/home/release.json (key) and tool/pack_home.dart refuses to pack with any other key or to mint a new one once that record exists. Accepted risk: losing the seed file means the next release cannot be signed as the same lineage; back it up (for example into 1Password, as scripts/pack-extension.sh does for the extension key) and restore it to the same path or CLAX_HOME_BUNDLE_KEY before packing.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":10},"end":{"line":27},"content_hash":"a684ed3d4ac165c88b36bd806663fcc26658e09d9b5b34d9e5d693ed1e92e26e"},"summary":"The shipped home app (apps/clax_app/assets/home/home.clax) is signed by a dedicated build-time Ed25519 key whose only copy is the seed file ~/.config/clax/home-bundle/key on the machine that packed it","tags":["signing","home-app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-clax.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:00:08.329118Z","id":"4730c5a245dc7ea03f3d9e05f3bafacc837bac5d58489ceef93466e0fc127b20","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"688a1a4ebb8462d93bf00159a978838a27eef14d5b16f26e7a891a1ed0598577","summary":"With Bazel the app's Android clax is //crates/clax-cli:clax_android_{arm64,x86_64}, always optimized and with the web UI embedded (bazel/android/clax.bzl), so this applies to the native build only (just app-clax-native android --debug).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-clax.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:00:08.329249Z","id":"695b9dc7e307a074d06d228f5e4c7c7c91b81fd1faee3815ee9f901b2372bff7","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"87888a6c851e5ee5685c4f01036464e501fb2d73299c977a5885e25f3de84ec2","summary":"With Bazel the NDK is fetched for the host by checksum, darwin or linux (android_ndk.configure in MODULE.bazel, bazel/android/rules_android_ndk.patch), so this applies to the native build only (just app-clax-native).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-home-bundle.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:27:16.237824Z","id":"83589be0d380e9ff8d385fad46591c375b7098377e8a1636629f6d69d687cb93","body":{"detail":"Why this key: lib/bundle/trust.dart decide() matches an installed app to a bundle by lineage AND author key, so every shipped release must carry the same key or installs treat it as a foreign lineage (no silent update). A key committed to the repository would let anyone sign a bundle on the home lineage that installs accept as an update of the home app, which holds the home capability; this install's own BundleKey (lib/platform/bundle_key.dart) differs per device, so it cannot sign a shared release. The public key is pinned as `key` in apps/clax_app/home/manifest.json, and tool/pack_home.dart (127-141) refuses to pack a release with any other key. Accepted risk: losing the seed file means the next release cannot be signed as the same lineage, and losing the ledger beside it (`releases`, tool/home-version.sh) restarts versions at the manifest's `version` + 1; back the directory up (for example into 1Password, as scripts/pack-extension.sh does for the extension key) and restore it to the same path or CLAX_HOME_BUNDLE_KEY before building.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":14},"end":{"line":22},"content_hash":"ce3fa6a1e9259d39bcd62faa6aae1e49aed8fe829555bd74ed272d87c846933e"},"summary":"The shipped home app (assets/home/home.clax, built by //apps/clax_app:home_bundle and this script) is signed by a dedicated build-time Ed25519 key whose only copy is the seed file ~/.config/clax/home-bundle/key on the machine that releases it","supersedes":"a58f4ba9d767c7e1ec9f1a6b575b672ae20c1443b3aa8d62cab5eedb8918d3d0","tags":["signing","home-app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-ios-spawns.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T04:59:32.393903Z","id":"1661f24fabf51ad340e5ece58d228eb3bfc66bd78d222ee5596115eca2c8ffef","body":{"detail":"scripts/ios-spawns.allow names a file and function per launch (crates/clax-core/src/gitctx.rs spawn, remote.rs process_started, clax-mcp channel.rs process_argv, tools.rs run_opener, clax-realtime push.rs run_queue); a new launch added to one of those functions, or a gate removed from one, passes. Whether the iOS arms compile is the job of a build of the daemon for aarch64-apple-ios (cargo check --target aarch64-apple-ios -p clax-server -p clax-mcp passes at 49a0cccabd27); whether they run nothing is reviewed per entry.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":54},"content_hash":"60ee3370d19e137bf7fee95f6ee65ab9988001ad220c8d9f2e36fa8ae30b0731"},"summary":"An allowed launch is trusted by its function name: the check does not read the cfg that keeps it off on iOS","tags":["revisit:a launch reaches iOS through an allowed function","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/sync-tokens.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:08:15.982316Z","id":"519517dd7c79fd92bbef52364f24c2463ecaaf79978e494b12da853958a9723c","body":{"detail":"kit_css rewrites only the text between tokens:begin and tokens:end, and kit_unguarded_mixes looks only for color-mix outside @supports. A later `:root { --k-bg: #fff }` below tokens:end wins by source order and --check still passes. design/tokens.json's contrast pairs also run only on the base palettes, never lightMore/darkMore (harmless while only border differs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":549},"end":{"line":583},"content_hash":"e7d7d1a902fa3cdf126a050ae808cdb277973cbcdbf5e4349971e0d1580278ba"},"suggested_fix":"Fail --check when a name in tokens.json's kit map is declared outside the region (allowing the documented --k-accent-soft @supports override).","summary":"The sync check does not notice a mapped --k-* token re-declared outside kit.css's markers, which silently overrides the brand","tags":["review","ui-phase-1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:09:36.137449Z","id":"44eecbbca2a89a4cd27c706402f4bc0e670d126f73f208aab6d00192de130304","body":{"detail":"scripts/check-no-unsafe.sh checks only the manifests and sources in its runfiles, and these two lists are written by hand. A new crate (crates/clax-ios included) that is not added to both passes //scripts:no_unsafe whatever it contains; only the native run (scripts/quality_gates.sh, which scans the checkout) sees it. scripts/bazel-sync.sh --check already fails on a crate without a BUILD.bazel; it could also fail on a crate absent from these lists, or the lists could be derived into bazel/workspace.bzl.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":76},"end":{"line":114},"content_hash":"1ccfcbf85f3d87164ea47ab017fa65cb482a58daf98f95cfb9ed960d36b23f95"},"summary":"A crate missing from RUST_SOURCES and CRATE_MANIFESTS is invisible to //scripts:no_unsafe under Bazel","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:16:43.345390Z","id":"2c524dd6d663c28fce0a8038d10d37d282d7e9654b7f7f0c6f9d563807c77158","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:49a0cccabd27","summary":"Fixed: clax-ios is in RUST_SOURCES and CRATE_MANIFESTS (scripts/BUILD.bazel), so the Bazel check reads its manifest and sources; bazelisk test //scripts:no_unsafe //scripts:crate_layers //scripts:ios_spawns: 3 PASSED, with crates/clax-ios/src/lib.rs's four exports present","supersedes":"44eecbbca2a89a4cd27c706402f4bc0e670d126f73f208aab6d00192de130304","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-ios-spawns.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:43:36.758751Z","id":"847d2ee95620ad014cd1bfe7ace76acbb3fe2d1b15fedf13af491c56ecb3efee","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"1661f24fabf51ad340e5ece58d228eb3bfc66bd78d222ee5596115eca2c8ffef","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":54},"content_hash":"60ee3370d19e137bf7fee95f6ee65ab9988001ad220c8d9f2e36fa8ae30b0731"},"summary":"The iOS arms now compile under Bazel in the test suite: //crates/clax-ios:ios_build_test builds clax-ios and its dependencies (clax-server, clax-mcp, clax-core, clax-realtime) for aarch64-apple-ios and aarch64-apple-ios-sim (bazelisk test //crates/clax-ios:ios_build_test: PASSED at 49a0cccabd27). Whether an allowed function runs nothing on iOS is still reviewed per entry.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-icons.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:44:20.267870Z","id":"aa0964b2abd3eb224e13c213ad2961bd29a44b7ad24990de4d89635fa1cca8e0","body":{"detail":"rules_flutter's flutter_macos_app (apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel :macos_app) defaults app_icons to macos/Runner/Assets.xcassets/AppIcon.appiconset and rules_apple refuses an .appiconset and a .icon together; the Xcode native twin does not list macos/Runner/AppIcon.icon in macos/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj. So macOS 26 shows the appiconset's light PNGs, with no dark or tinted appearance. actool from Xcode 26.6 compiles AppIcon.icon alone at --minimum-deployment-target 12.0 into Assets.car and an AppIcon.icns fallback (xcrun actool --compile OUT --platform macosx --minimum-deployment-target 12.0 --app-icon AppIcon … AppIcon.icon), so passing app_icons = glob([\"macos/Runner/AppIcon.icon/**\"]) and adding the bundle to the Xcode project could ship it to every supported macOS, at the cost of 12–15 drawing the system's fallback rather than the appiconset's shadowed body. Which icon source macOS builds ship is the owner's call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":363},"end":{"line":415},"content_hash":"67a50b0ac3f9d545a83e9aca334b0d1f12dc71e19fca728cb223088d4849c0ef"},"summary":"AppIcon.icon is rendered and committed, but neither build ships it","tags":["status:needs-decision","revisit:macOS dark or tinted app icons wanted","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-icons.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:00:02.013360Z","id":"aef420802d9b9985f3b545562f90677ca5ab530f7f3217a22ee5f11b38a03f8f","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/res/drawable/splash_mark.xml carries design/mark.json's paths scaled to 132 dp on a 288 dp canvas, and res/values/clax_colors.xml and values-night/clax_colors.xml carry tokens.json's bg, you, agent and fg. TARGETS here does not write them and --check (//design:icons_sync) does not cover them, so a changed mark or token updates the icons and ClaxSplash but leaves the splash stale.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":419},"end":{"line":419},"content_hash":"3054ea691a777a173857add059250d5c4f3a2038f5e2160868e6047c9edfc050"},"suggested_fix":"Add a splash target to TARGETS that writes splash_mark.xml and both clax_colors.xml with the GENERATED header, so --check covers them.","summary":"The Android splash's mark and colours are copied by hand, not rendered from design/mark.json and design/tokens.json","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/sync-tokens.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:13:52.253603Z","id":"109b75d575cf63ac9d165864461cd0d946bdeb6525106a057d4b332dbca1a95a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:49a0cccabd27","summary":"kit_redeclared fails a mapped --k-* declared outside the region and outside @supports, and contrast pairs run on the more-contrast palettes. Cases 13 and 16 of scripts/test-sync-tokens.sh: `bazelisk test //scripts:sync_tokens //design:tokens_sync` PASSED.","supersedes":"519517dd7c79fd92bbef52364f24c2463ecaaf79978e494b12da853958a9723c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-copy.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:21:34.315462Z","id":"31e0a7591c99f643f99d2a1550f467c4ca5065534d122e5ebf21512b1842aafc","body":{"detail":"So htm attributes (title=\"Nothing here\"), JSON in a literal and CSS or regex text mostly pass without an allow comment, at the cost that a quoted phrase right after other punctuation (—\"word\", /\"word\") passes unchecked. Apostrophes, three dots and raw errors are not heuristic in this way.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":41},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"2d529250efa58294284943b50756999ca2a4a62962492103df1fc052f7a1ee4b"},"summary":"The straight-quotes rule is a heuristic: it counts a \" or ' only after the literal's start, a space or a bracket, and skips literals that open with { or [","tags":["copy","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-icons.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:31:00.126540Z","id":"2ae8e8b71d248b34c8470dd058aff71e62e5e8b8f55ecf905fdd55eb0b239330","body":{"detail":"app_icon_16.png is apple_svg(16, 'light'): the 560-in-1024 mark becomes about 9 px wide, so the 1.7-radius dot and the 2.6 stroke arcs share pixels (target/flutter-app/shots/icons/mac-light-16-nn.png). Finder's list view, Spotlight and the Dock's small sizes show this one. Android's mdpi 48 px legacy icon still separates the three shapes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":348},"end":{"line":351},"content_hash":"94455d049bd50c032a30ace16611e598d81c7e8fd9147f56efc9808cc30dfea8"},"suggested_fix":"Draw the 16 px slot (and check 32) with a small-size variant (larger mark in the body, the dot and the gaps snapped to whole pixels), or check them on a Mac and record the call.","summary":"The 16 px macOS icon is the 1024 design scaled down: the dot fuses with both arcs into a grey bar and the mark reads as “>-<”","tags":["review","icons","phase-2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-icons.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:46:02.697958Z","id":"772a7d45e0b84a085ffb5fe2f32e3f51ea7430fe42bc01a4f9112cdd2c512e87","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:49a0cccabd27","summary":"Fixed: APPLE_SMALL draws app_icon_16.png and app_icon_32.png with a 704/640-wide mark of shallower arcs, a stroke of 3 and a dot of radius 2, about 1.5 px between each arc and the dot at 16 px. scripts/build-app-icons.sh --preview renders mac-{light,dark}-{16,32,64}.png: arc, gap, dot, gap, arc in both themes; bazelisk test //design:icons_sync passes.","supersedes":"2ae8e8b71d248b34c8470dd058aff71e62e5e8b8f55ecf905fdd55eb0b239330","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/app-iphone.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:42:12.189672Z","id":"66eb869f11677352b02c0309b9f7e702dfa1f1dba63242ebacbf416ca10745aa","body":{"detail":"No signing inputs, device or App Store Connect key exist on this machine yet, so these steps were never run for real. The command shapes come from Xcode 26.6's own help: altool 26.40.1 documents `--upload-package <ipa> --api-key <ID> --api-issuer <ID>` (no `--type`; the legacy `--apiKey`/`--apiIssuer` spelling is behind `--use-old-altool`), and `devicectl device info files` only lists a container, so daemon.json is read with `devicectl device copy from --domain-type appDataContainer`. The launched PID is read from `devicectl device process launch --json-output` at result.process.processIdentifier, and devices from `devicectl list devices --json-output` (hardwareProperties.platform, connectionProperties.pairingState and tunnelState), key paths not yet seen on a real device's output.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":284},"end":{"line":351},"content_hash":"f417eeba9adf4f4a2f23290504679c72de20b83be6fe4781ac9487f19d4fa4f4"},"suggested_fix":"On the first device build and the first TestFlight upload, run scripts/app-iphone.sh (dry run, then --i-know-what-i-am-doing) and fix any key path or flag that differs; then resolve this.","summary":"The device install, launch and daemon.json read, and the altool upload, have run only against the stubs of scripts/test-app-iphone.sh","tags":["ios","testflight","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-no-unsafe.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:42:06.460474Z","id":"e2012d4a41ccdfc5636abd6f5b0d2b52ef6f9e3f2d4539898428cea223bb8a01","body":{"detail":"Two shapes pass the check (scripts/check-no-unsafe.sh run on a copy of Cargo.toml, crates/clax-embed/Cargo.toml and crates/clax-embed/src/ffi.rs, exit 0 for each): (1) in the body of `pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn clax_embed_open`, a line `let _b = Box::from_raw(home.as_ptr() as *mut [u8; 4]);` with no unsafe block. Edition 2024 makes `unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn` a warning, not an error (`rustc --edition 2024` on such a function prints `warning[E0133]: call to unsafe function ... requires unsafe block` and exits 0), and the crate's lint flags (bazel/workspace.bzl crates/clax-embed lint_flags, crates/clax-embed/Cargo.toml [lints.rust]) do not deny it; the script only looks for lines with the word `unsafe`. (2) `pub extern \"C\" fn clax_embed_close(core: u64) -> i32 { unsafe { *(core as *mut u8) = 0 }; crate::ffi_close(core) }` on one line: the whole signature line ($i + 1) is granted. scripts/test-check-no-unsafe.sh even has a passing case \"an export on one line\". Today clippy's -Dwarnings (`--config=clippy` in scripts/bazel-test.sh) catches (1) and the rustfmt check catches (2), so `just ci` holds, but spec 2026-10-19 §14 says //scripts:no_unsafe itself fails on any other unsafe, a second from_raw_parts and Box::from_raw.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":123},"end":{"line":146},"content_hash":"d2bc47a735b12808f77405876e2ddd24e46f9df99c51479618c63a6715bb7937"},"suggested_fix":"Add `unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn = \"forbid\"` to crates/clax-embed/Cargo.toml [lints.rust] (and -Funsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn to its lint_flags via just bazel-sync), have the check require it, and grant only a signature line that ends at its `(` or `{` (nothing after the opening brace); add both shapes as failing cases in scripts/test-check-no-unsafe.sh.","summary":"//scripts:no_unsafe passes an unsafe operation in clax-embed's exports that carries no `unsafe` keyword, and any code on a granted signature line","tags":["review","unsafe","embed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-no-unsafe.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:32:05.111159Z","id":"f2f42cbb7f4f77c557b7cf62b8700f493fa8cb3a86dcc119413f46e286238f2d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:49a0cccabd27","summary":"Fixed in 49a0cccabd27: crates/clax-embed/Cargo.toml forbids unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn (bazel/workspace.bzl lint_flags -Funsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn), the check fails without it, and a signature line is granted only up to its `(`. //scripts:no_unsafe_test passes with the new cases 'unsafe after the brace of an export on one line', 'unsafe after the brace of a signature line', 'an unsafe operation with no unsafe block, the lint not forbidden' and 'clax-embed only denying unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn', all of which failed against the old check; `rustc --edition 2024 -Funsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn` on Box::from_raw in an unsafe fn body now errors E0133.","supersedes":"e2012d4a41ccdfc5636abd6f5b0d2b52ef6f9e3f2d4539898428cea223bb8a01","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/patch-pub.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:39:08.878040Z","id":"3d901cf2ba8e71090d93ab5d0c9271d623e6611d0d71097365b936cf824d1b3e","body":{"detail":"Only its dry run was run. scripts/run.sh's native app-integration and app-macos run it, then flutter with PUB_CACHE at that directory; whether flutter pub get --enforce-lockfile leaves pubspec.lock unchanged with a private PUB_CACHE, and whether the native macOS build compiles the patched plugin, are unverified.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":24},"end":{"line":66},"content_hash":"6289bfde1e17533e4f8005d4c524b092cdbf33ed2ff4e2f3dac28fd63832ee14"},"summary":"patch-pub.sh's acting run (flutter pub get into apps/clax_app/build-native/pub-cache, then the patch) has not been run, nor the native recipes that call it","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/app-android-emulator.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:18:26.371055Z","id":"5abbf5a5856d48ac87240afb0b5c876b5037b0a6838fb2d9c3b208805b878c9f","body":{"detail":"target/android-avd/Clax_Pixel.running keeps only the serial and PID. If the emulator dies without --stop (a crash, a reboot, a test killed by Bazel's timeout) and the PID is later reused, running_one reports that process; --start prints 'already running' with its PID, and --stop sends adb emu kill (no effect), waits up to 60 s while the process lives, then kill PID (lines 269-275).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":176},"end":{"line":182},"content_hash":"b2e09b9a96c4ea25bb2e58719bdd767fadc9cc6cc9b8f685ded0687436b5faad"},"suggested_fix":"Write the process's start time and command (ps -o lstart= -o comm= -p PID) beside the PID at start, and have running_one compare both before reporting or stopping; otherwise remove the file and report nothing running.","summary":"The emulator's PID is trusted by kill -0 alone: a stale .running file and a reused PID make --start report a stranger as the emulator and --stop kill it after 60 s","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/app-android-emulator.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:18:26.371085Z","id":"31561f1121a4b35b580d3d41fdcc408ed33410559201aed58cd8f83e2e11e081","body":{"detail":"The early-exit branch (lines 231-236) removes the .running file but never runs adb kill-server on ANDROID_ADB_SERVER_PORT, so an adb server of this script outlives it. There is no trap, so SIGINT or SIGTERM during the boot wait leaves the backgrounded emulator and its adb server running with no record of who owns them once .running is stale. A private adb server still enumerates USB devices, so whether it contends with the owner's adb on 5037 for a plugged-in phone is unverified.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":216},"end":{"line":248},"content_hash":"a409225ba847869cdd01ae909bb0ae4fd54adf56418fb5593ea9aa43c2d1d5f0"},"suggested_fix":"trap on EXIT/INT/TERM in --start that, unless boot succeeded, stops the PID it started and runs adb kill-server on its port; verify with a phone plugged in that adb -P 5037 devices keeps it 'device' while the emulator runs.","summary":"--start cleans up only on its 300 s timeout: an emulator that exits while booting leaves its adb server on port+10000, and an interrupt during the wait leaves the emulator running","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/app-android-emulator.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:18:26.371111Z","id":"c0e0d9f797ba3393cce36adf41e7a06641f838153db0074c7432416b4b1bafd1","body":{"detail":"fastboot.forceColdBoot=yes, -no-snapshot and tool/android-integration-run.sh's uninstall before each install mean no run reuses the AVD's data, yet target/android-avd/Clax_Pixel.avd/userdata-qemu.img.qcow2 was 1.3 GB here, per worktree, up to the 6G data partition. The system image is shared: Bazel 9.3's repository contents cache links external/+http_archive+android_system_image into ~/Library/Caches/bazel/_bazel_alex/cache/repos/v1/contents (4.3 GB unpacked, once per user, plus its 1.7 GB zip in content_addressable), so docs/bazel.md's 'unpacks the system image into the output base' overstates the per-worktree cost.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":141},"end":{"line":163},"content_hash":"94fd14d0fce85130f34d4f4d3c14155f341fef3552eb6c676e5c941527260bfd"},"suggested_fix":"Boot with -read-only (writes go to temporary files removed at exit, so the AVD neither grows nor locks, and runs in two worktrees could share one AVD); add --clean that removes target/android-avd, target/android-home and target/android-sdk; correct docs/bazel.md's disk note.","summary":"Each worktree's AVD keeps a writable data image that grows (1.3 GB in this worktree after one run) though nothing in it is reused","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/app-macos-dev.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:18:26.371136Z","id":"67b692abc6583acd375a8de32b532ba314b3c0559b3787b50642692397dd94d4","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/SchemeHost.swift sets FWFWebViewFlutterWKWebViewExternalAPI.configurationHook, which only configuration-hook.patch adds. scripts/run.sh's native app-integration and app-macos run scripts/patch-pub.sh and set PUB_CACHE to apps/clax_app/build-native/pub-cache; app-macos-dev.sh (the hot-reload loop, docs/usage.md:715) does neither.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":44},"content_hash":"054c9ceeaff81fddc73e1a604ba9cae06fe9cf77d172618290f729c6cddb4b80"},"suggested_fix":"Run ./scripts/patch-pub.sh --i-know-what-i-am-doing in app-macos-dev.sh's steps and exec flutter run with PUB_CACHE at that directory, and list the step in its dry run.","summary":"just app-macos-dev runs flutter run with the unpatched webview_flutter_wkwebview, which has no configurationHook, so the Mac runner no longer compiles there","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:07:20.175030Z","id":"3f49bc3f0b54ab4be6464a90a43164074c7f7bffcff8f8ba58a8d4a19ffa4868","body":{"detail":"//apps/clax_app:macos_app at 49a0cccabd27, launched with a scratch CLAX_APP_DIR: a sample of the app showed its flutter_secure_storage queue in SecItemCopyMatching -> SecKeychainItemCopyContent for the whole run, ioreg reported CGSSessionScreenIsLocked = Yes, the daemon was never spawned and no timings.jsonl was written. scripts/perf-app-launch.sh --macos --runs 1 --i-know-what-i-am-doing reported both launches missing (60 s cap each), stopped each app by PID and removed its scratch directory. The --android path (lines 266-313) has not run against a device or emulator either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":44},"end":{"line":47},"content_hash":"e29ac5cd957152be85b7473e1e7fc9c97776068ce8f69d0ff8decb6170d348d6"},"suggested_fix":"With the screen unlocked: CLAX_PERF_JSON=target/perf/app-launch-before.json scripts/perf-app-launch.sh --macos --record --i-know-what-i-am-doing, answering Always Allow on the first launch's keychain prompt; then scripts/perf-log.sh record target/perf/app-launch-before.json, and commit web/perf/budget.json. On the phone, with its owner present, the same with --android after just app-phone.","summary":"No launch baseline is recorded and web/perf/budget.json has no app_home_usable_ms or app_home_cover_ms budget: every macOS launch of the ad hoc signed daemon build waited on the login keychain prompt for the saved API key while the screen was locked","tags":["time-to-usable","needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:18:11.920109Z","id":"f729ccc3cbe0db5380c388921f1fced9153dd0382f7384e0fb064750e22ed66d","body":{"detail":"Failure: scripts/perf-app-launch.sh --macos --i-know-what-i-am-doing on a real build (or --android). The macOS loop SIGTERMs the app as soon as the count of home-usable lines grows (lines 236-244); the Android loop force-stops it at the next iteration's start (line 296) right after the same check. HomeSnapshotter takes the snapshot only 3 s after a shown load (apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_snapshot.dart:262 settle, updated() at 310-317) or when home is covered or put in the background; SIGTERM and am force-stop run neither. The scratch CLAX_APP_DIR is new on each script run, so <dir>/cache/home/home-snapshot.bin never exists: every launch takes the no-snapshot path, home-cover is never written, the JSON reports app_home_cover_ms runs 0 with missing equal to the run count, --record writes no cover budget, and the dropped launch drops nothing that differs from the others. docs/usage.md (\"Measuring the home screen's start\") itself says to leave the home screen up for a second before the next launch. The fake app in scripts/test-perf-app-launch.sh:96-120 writes home-cover from a script, so the test passes regardless.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":231},"end":{"line":245},"content_hash":"01647a0a64d1d224c1553d0bb1087531679fe774f7b6b966f4555d46b39a0b6c"},"suggested_fix":"After the dropped launch's home-usable, wait (a bounded loop on the condition, e.g. 30 s) for <scratch>/cache/home/home-snapshot.bin to exist before stopping the app, and stop the run with a message if it never appears; on Android the same with `run-as dev.empathic.clax ls cache/home/home-snapshot.bin`. Make the fake app write home-cover only when a snapshot file exists and write that file a moment after home-usable, so the test fails on the current loop.","summary":"Each launch is stopped the moment home-usable is written, before the home screen's snapshot is taken, so no launch ever has a snapshot: app_home_cover_ms is never measured and every home-usable is a launch without its cover","tags":["review","time-to-usable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:18:11.920218Z","id":"f8e77ca85d183cc41ea0defc352026e3dd581ab3af4e9bccd9d9f335cd5dfc6d","body":{"detail":"CLAX_APP_DIR (apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart:104-117) moves only the support and cache directories. The executable runs as dev.empathic.clax, so everything else lands in ~/Library/Containers/dev.empathic.clax/Data, the container of the owner's installed app: AppKit's frame autosave rewrites 'NSWindow Frame ClaxMain' in Data/Library/Preferences/dev.empathic.clax.plist (on this Mac that file was last written at 06:53 on 2026-10-20, when Data/Library/Caches/flutter_engine was also made); once a launch reaches the home screen, WKWebView keeps localStorage, IndexedDB and the clax_key_<port> cookie of each scratch daemon's origins (http://127.0.0.1:<port>, http://<id>.localhost:<port>) in the container's default website data store, which the owner's app shares, and a scratch port that equals the installed app's kept port (its daemon-port, 57053 on this Mac, when that app is not running) shares an origin with the owner's pages. Answering Always Allow adds the measured build's ad hoc signature to the ACL of the owner's saved API key (flutter_secure_storage, login keychain: apps/clax_app/lib/platform/secure_key.dart), and that build reads the real key. Restoring the plist afterwards is unreliable while cfprefsd caches it and the installed app may be running.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":191},"end":{"line":233},"content_hash":"7aca189c46c14623130fac1d9e099f121c56a239b8e417d23475cea8d2815cfb"},"suggested_fix":"Unpack the measured app, set CFBundleIdentifier to dev.empathic.clax.perf in its Info.plist and re-sign the outer bundle ad hoc keeping its entitlements (codesign --force --sign - --preserve-metadata=entitlements,flags,runtime, without identifier), so it runs in a container of its own that the script deletes at the end; check first that the sandbox names the container by the new identifier. The keychain ACL write stays (the item is the owner's), unless the measured run is given no key. The owner decides whether a re-identified copy is a faithful measure.","summary":"A measured macOS run writes into the owner's own app container: the window frame default, WebKit website data and cookies, Flutter's engine cache, and on Always Allow the keychain item's ACL","tags":["review","time-to-usable","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:18:11.920261Z","id":"8c98876b6e103519553d2fe0c008cfe0e74f81577858f1136db9bd08ad97ac5a","body":{"detail":"With the screen locked or a keychain prompt waiting, every launch waits out the cap: `just perf` on a Mac (scripts/run.sh _perf_app_launch) then spends about (N+1) x 60 s, 10 minutes at the default 9, to report nothing. When only some launches are missing, `missing` appears in the stdout JSON (line 121) but not in the CLAX_PERF_JSON lines (lines 128-136), and --record (lines 142-154) writes a budget from however many launches finished, which is then never rewritten (--record skips a platform's existing budgets).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":236},"end":{"line":243},"content_hash":"cfd6daefd9153a0161ebb6435ad08e4a9092a43c7d450238d7b5fb19ab80f6d9"},"suggested_fix":"Stop after the dropped launch when it gives no home-usable (a lock or a prompt does not clear by itself), and check ioreg's CGSSessionScreenIsLocked before the first launch; refuse --record when app_home_usable_ms.missing or app_home_cover_ms.missing is above 0; write the missing count as its own perf-log line.","summary":"A launch that times out costs its full 60 s and the run goes on, and the summary, the perf-log lines and --record treat a partial run like a full one","tags":["review","time-to-usable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:18:11.920293Z","id":"f595e91d68eb4e37f90fdb7eedf76158710dfb00fe1fd21d20ecade5f7d04584","body":{"detail":"The summary (lines 116-155) names only the platform. scripts/perf-log.sh record stamps `git rev-parse HEAD` of the checkout it runs in (scripts/perf-log.sh:39-40, PERF_COMMIT set there, overriding any value in the environment). The daemon baseline that spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md section 12 asks for has to come from a build before the core lands, measured with this script's --app from a later checkout, so its perf-log record names the wrong commit, and the app's clax reports clax_commit 'unknown' (the fixture's audit rows, crates/clax-embed/tests/fixtures/homes/flutter-app-43.sql:302-317), so the build cannot tell either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":209},"end":{"line":225},"content_hash":"4793510c7101664f4f30934486d04c8a6176af0ae363ddd9a3fd76e73bbd3c1e"},"suggested_fix":"Add an \"app\" object to the JSON (the bundle path, the zip's sha256 that line 215 already computes, and the bundle's CFBundleVersion) and a --commit <sha> label written into each perf-log line's name or a field; let scripts/perf-log.sh record take PERF_COMMIT from the environment when set.","summary":"Nothing records which build was measured: with --app, the figures and scripts/perf-log.sh's record are attributed to the checkout's HEAD, not to the app","tags":["review","time-to-usable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:18:11.920326Z","id":"76129aca76494b5d10b4a802df78628eb12ad8704277fc8fa46ed4601641233c","body":{"detail":"--record writes all_budgets[platform] = {\"app_home_usable_ms\": …, \"app_home_cover_ms\": …}. usable.perf.ts keys the same file by `${platform()}-${arch()}` and treats any entry as its Budget: judge() takes `b = all[PLATFORM] ?? null` (line 318), so b is no longer null, its 'no baseline, report only' branch is skipped, and b.baseline[mode] (line 324) or b.control[mode] (line 346) throws a TypeError. Only darwin-arm64 has a web entry today, so an Intel Mac (darwin-x64) is the case; Android keys (android-<model>) never match Node's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":142},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"2a6d079174cd789a9e65ee5e6e574635582d813f7573723d54b6ddfc4b9d59ed"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the app's budgets apart from the web ones (a top-level \"app\" object keyed by platform, or web/perf/app-budget.json), or have usable.perf.ts treat an entry without `baseline` as no budget.","summary":"--record on a platform with no web budget makes an entry that web/perf/usable.perf.ts then reads as a full Budget and fails on","tags":["review","time-to-usable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:18:11.920985Z","id":"bf85f4c573d21a63ada4e059ebf0e39b3c4255aadfdc979320de4b256ccd5c0c","body":{"detail":"(1) `scripts/perf-log.sh record <metrics>` only prints the record; `--append target/perf-log.jsonl` keeps it (scripts/perf-log.sh:7-11), and the record names the checkout's HEAD, so run it from a checkout of the measured build's commit. (2) The macOS measure can be taken after the core lands from a build of the parent of the commit that puts the app on the core: build //apps/clax_app:macos_app at that commit from a clean checkout, keep its zip under target/perf/, and run this script from the current checkout with --app <zip> (the zip is unpacked once by content under target/perf/app-<sha12>, and its ad hoc signature stays the same, so one Always Allow serves every run of it). The snapshot blocker on lines 231-245 of this script has to be fixed first or app_home_cover_ms comes out empty. (3) This branch's build carries migrations past the installed homes' 43 (crates/clax-embed/tests/old_homes.rs asserts the open ends at JOBS_MIGRATION, 46), and spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md section 10.2 forbids installing such a build on the owner's devices before the last task copies and checks their homes. --android measures the installed app against the phone's real home, so the phone's daemon baseline is the build installed now, measured without `just app-phone`.","kind":"comment","references":"3f49bc3f0b54ab4be6464a90a43164074c7f7bffcff8f8ba58a8d4a19ffa4868","summary":"The baseline's procedure needs three corrections: append to the perf log with --append, measure the daemon build with --app after the core lands, and take the phone's baseline on the installed build without just app-phone","tags":["review","time-to-usable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:41:03.074244Z","id":"344145cc322008054ede5842b4f592c81814881ea5f8f97f1fd1fa152dfe4501","body":{"detail":"Checked on 2026-10-20 with the screen locked: target/perf/app-ebea9c8c387b/Clax.app copied with ditto, CFBundleIdentifier set to dev.empathic.clax.perf, signed with codesign --force --sign - --preserve-metadata=entitlements,flags,runtime (codesign -dv: Identifier=dev.empathic.clax.perf, Signature=adhoc, app-sandbox kept; codesign --verify --deep --strict passed). Launched once by its Contents/MacOS/Clax: the sandbox made ~/Library/Containers/dev.empathic.clax.perf within 1.5 s, with Data/Library/Application Support/dev.empathic.clax.perf (install-id, clax-home/config.toml) and Data/Library/Caches/dev.empathic.clax.perf and flutter_engine; ~/Library/Containers/dev.empathic.clax/Data/Library/Preferences/dev.empathic.clax.plist kept its mtime. A sample of the copy showed its main work in SecItemCopyMatching -> SecKeychainItemCopyContent, as record 3f49bc3f saw for the dev.empathic.clax build: flutter_secure_storage_darwin 0.4.3 queries the login keychain (usesDataProtectionKeychain false, apps/clax_app/lib/platform/secure_key.dart) by service flutter_secure_storage_service and account anthropic_api_key, with no bundle ID in the query, so the copy matches the item the installed app saved and macOS asks whether to let it read it. No timings.jsonl and no daemon: DaemonSupervisor starts the daemon only after apiKey() returns (apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart _keyOrNull). The copy was stopped by its PID and its container removed. Without a saved key the read returns null at once and the daemon starts with sample() off (_keyOrNull; nothing else on the way to the home screen needs the key), so home-usable would be written: the measure needs the copy to read no key, not a key. The scripted agent mode (--dart-define=CLAX_SCRIPTED_AGENT, lib/main.dart:54-59) is no way round: it is debug-only and replaces only the agent backend, while the supervisor still reads secureKey.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":27},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"ef00e59479f29f8fa1f9ccbb53956e2121ab6f907df48da58385f672d22e5bcc"},"suggested_fix":"Options for the owner: (a) the app reads no key when its environment says so, e.g. CLAX_APP_NO_KEY=1 making main.dart's secureKey a store with no key, set by scripts/perf-app-launch.sh; the daemon baseline then needs that change on the pre-core build too (the parent of Task 17's commit plus that commit, built in a checkout the owner makes); (b) query by bundle ID (MacOsOptions accountName set to the bundle identifier), which moves the installed app's own key to a new item and needs a one-time copy of the old one; (c) answer the question for the copy at each run (Deny gives a null key but adds the wait to every launch's home-usable; Always Allow adds the copy's ad hoc signature to the saved key's ACL, the write record f8e77ca8 named).","summary":"The re-identified copy dev.empathic.clax.perf still asks for the installed app's saved API key: the login keychain is not kept per container, so a measured launch waits on macOS's keychain question","tags":["review","time-to-usable","needs-device","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:43:04.833792Z","id":"9bbe2b8da5103d265260a25923fd4b813dfa7ee634c26679551e7aaa05da7dec","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f8e77ca85d183cc41ea0defc352026e3dd581ab3af4e9bccd9d9f335cd5dfc6d","summary":"Decided by the owner, 2026-10-20: measure a re-identified copy. The script's unpacked copy gets CFBundleIdentifier dev.empathic.clax.perf and is signed again ad hoc keeping its entitlements, so it runs in a container of its own; the script deletes that container at the end; it never touches dev.empathic.clax's container or the owner's saved key.","tags":["status:decided","time-to-usable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:43:04.834120Z","id":"1181540ffce67114d5e3e819437f079a2e2a44074742d57f6b64bc9342223c42","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:49a0cccabd27","summary":"Done as the owner decided on 2026-10-20, in 49a0cccabd27: scripts/perf-app-launch.sh --macos copies the build under target/perf/clax-perf-<sha>, sets the copy's CFBundleIdentifier to dev.empathic.clax.perf, signs it again with codesign --force --sign - --preserve-metadata=entitlements,flags,runtime, runs it without CLAX_APP_DIR, removes ~/Library/Containers/dev.empathic.clax.perf before the first launch and at the end, and refuses a CLAX_PERF_CONTAINER of another name. bazelisk test //scripts:perf_app_launch_test passes (19 checks), among them '--macos: the copy, never the app given, is re-identified as dev.empathic.clax.perf and signed again keeping its entitlements; it runs without CLAX_APP_DIR', '--macos: the copy's container is removed before the first launch and at the end' and 'a container not named dev.empathic.clax.perf is refused before any launch'. One launch of a re-identified local build showed the sandbox making ~/Library/Containers/dev.empathic.clax.perf, and dev.empathic.clax's preferences plist kept its mtime. The keychain part does not hold: the copy still asks for the installed app's saved key item, record 344145cc.","supersedes":"f8e77ca85d183cc41ea0defc352026e3dd581ab3af4e9bccd9d9f335cd5dfc6d","tags":["reason:fixed","time-to-usable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:43:18.997517Z","id":"eda17cb293fe16c6aa64f0bffbb5f25d628087b3470e809e2a5329540793e816","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:49a0cccabd27","summary":"Fixed in 49a0cccabd27: after the dropped launch's home-usable, scripts/perf-app-launch.sh waits (at most the cap) for <container>/Data/Library/Caches/dev.empathic.clax.perf/home/home-snapshot.bin on macOS and for run-as dev.empathic.clax ls cache/home/home-snapshot.bin on Android before stopping the app, and stops the run when none is kept. The test's fake app now writes home-cover only when a snapshot exists and takes it a second after home-usable; before the fix its loop printed app_home_cover_ms runs 0, missing 3, and after it bazelisk test //scripts:perf_app_launch_test passes with '--macos: four launches for three runs, the first dropped once its snapshot is kept, so each measured launch has its cover' (cover median 25, p90 30, runs 3, missing 0) and 'a dropped launch that keeps no snapshot within the cap stops the run before any measured launch'.","supersedes":"f729ccc3cbe0db5380c388921f1fced9153dd0382f7384e0fb064750e22ed66d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:43:19.518411Z","id":"547d2e8d48293a2adde3ae309c0c988d67555653553d5e258f27d175ebe8608a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:49a0cccabd27","summary":"Fixed in 49a0cccabd27: --macos stops before the first launch while ioreg reports CGSSessionScreenIsLocked=Yes; on both platforms a dropped launch without home-usable within the cap stops the run; with CLAX_PERF_JSON each timing's missing count is its own perf-log line (unit launches); --record exits 1 and writes nothing when any launch is missing. bazelisk test //scripts:perf_app_launch_test passes with 'a locked screen (CGSSessionScreenIsLocked) stops the run before any launch', 'a dropped launch without home-usable stops the run after one launch, its app stopped', 'CLAX_PERF_JSON: each median and p90 for perf-log.sh, the p90s beside their budgets, and the launches missing' and '--record refuses a run with a launch missing and writes nothing'; each failed before the change.","supersedes":"8c98876b6e103519553d2fe0c008cfe0e74f81577858f1136db9bd08ad97ac5a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:43:20.026010Z","id":"9772b92be3fb9fb2827f2032562e2cce82f3454c9ea0697f791cdef3799b0327","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:49a0cccabd27","summary":"Fixed in 49a0cccabd27: the JSON gains build {commit (--commit, else HEAD when the script built the app), app, sha256, version (CFBundleShortVersionString (CFBundleVersion), or versionName (versionCode) on Android)}, and scripts/perf-log.sh record stamps PERF_COMMIT when set. bazelisk test //scripts:perf_app_launch_test passes with '--macos: the JSON names the build measured: --commit, the app, its digest and its version', 'five launches: ... the build named by --commit' and 'perf-log.sh record names PERF_COMMIT's build'.","supersedes":"f595e91d68eb4e37f90fdb7eedf76158710dfb00fe1fd21d20ecade5f7d04584","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:43:20.542749Z","id":"df49b2fb29ece62068922a20ce19dfd192e02a3aa54a254af67631eb7be9f026","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:49a0cccabd27","summary":"Fixed in 49a0cccabd27: scripts/perf-app-launch.sh reads and records its budgets in web/perf/app-budget.json (created empty), so web/perf/usable.perf.ts's file holds web budgets only. bazelisk test //scripts:perf_app_launch_test passes with 'the app's budgets are kept in web/perf/app-budget.json, apart from the web's budget.json that usable.perf.ts reads', which failed before the change.","supersedes":"76129aca76494b5d10b4a802df78628eb12ad8704277fc8fa46ed4601641233c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:43:37.728230Z","id":"394cf9a6e13c0695e24b16d8f217fedaae8bee9f8c230d25e368f9f8028c9b18","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:49a0cccabd27","summary":"Fixed in 49a0cccabd27: docs/usage.md ('Measuring the home screen's start', 'Taking the launch baseline') and plan Task 16 Step 5 (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-19-in-process-core.md) now append with scripts/perf-log.sh record --append target/perf-log.jsonl under PERF_COMMIT=<the measured build's commit> (PERF_COMMIT honoured since 49a0cccabd27), measure the daemon build's zip with --app and --commit from this checkout (built in a checkout the owner makes; an agent makes none), and take the phone's baseline on the installed build without just app-phone. Record 3f49bc3f's fix is rewritten to the same procedure.","supersedes":"bf85f4c573d21a63ada4e059ebf0e39b3c4255aadfdc979320de4b256ccd5c0c","tags":["reason:fixed","time-to-usable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:43:37.784410Z","id":"b2ec527c930657a3dd5a08a218f3822ec9970d4da107504d6be9c0fa8b05261c","body":{"detail":"//apps/clax_app:macos_app at 49a0cccabd27, launched with a scratch CLAX_APP_DIR: a sample of the app showed its flutter_secure_storage queue in SecItemCopyMatching -> SecKeychainItemCopyContent for the whole run, ioreg reported CGSSessionScreenIsLocked = Yes, the daemon was never spawned and no timings.jsonl was written. The script now stops at once on a locked screen (49a0cccabd27) and measures a copy re-identified as dev.empathic.clax.perf (49a0cccabd27), which still asks for the same saved key item (record 344145cc, an open decision): the macOS baseline waits on that decision. The --android path has not run against a device or emulator either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":64},"end":{"line":68},"content_hash":"4cf41a9b319ed9aaa140b7946796968e332f4a4e5154ae8deb13c76e5a65be8d"},"suggested_fix":"The owner's steps in docs/usage.md ('Taking the launch baseline'): name the daemon build's commit C (the branch head before Task 17 lands, else the parent of Task 17's commit); build its zip with just app-macos in a checkout of C the owner makes and keep it as target/perf/clax-macos-$C.zip; with the screen unlocked and record 344145cc decided, CLAX_PERF_JSON=target/perf/app-launch-before.json scripts/perf-app-launch.sh --macos --app target/perf/clax-macos-$C.zip --commit $C --runs 9 --record --i-know-what-i-am-doing; then PERF_COMMIT=$C scripts/perf-log.sh record --append target/perf-log.jsonl target/perf/app-launch-before.json. On the phone, with its owner present, the build installed now (never just app-phone): --android --commit <its commit> --record, logged the same way. Commit web/perf/app-budget.json with both runs' medians and p90s.","summary":"No launch baseline is recorded and web/perf/app-budget.json has no app_home_usable_ms or app_home_cover_ms budget: every macOS launch of the ad hoc signed daemon build waited on the login keychain prompt for the saved API key while the screen was locked","supersedes":"3f49bc3f0b54ab4be6464a90a43164074c7f7bffcff8f8ba58a8d4a19ffa4868","tags":["time-to-usable","needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:55:07.581680Z","id":"b68a172975f245bb760f609416bf8544b0a7d4253d715613ff9a9d27b8d90079","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"344145cc322008054ede5842b4f592c81814881ea5f8f97f1fd1fa152dfe4501","summary":"Decided by the owner, Alex Kesling, on 2026-10-20: option (a). With CLAX_APP_NO_KEY=1 in its environment the app reads no saved API key (no keychain access at all, as if none were saved), so a launch measure never touches the owner's key and never prompts.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:55:07.581966Z","id":"c1306f84060d6b5e3d08af1b65d21b9b37e1bc461e42a445b99a0d72d6aba193","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:49a0cccabd27","summary":"Done as decided, in 49a0cccabd27: FlutterSecureKey (apps/clax_app/lib/platform/secure_key.dart) takes withheld, set in platformServices (apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart) from FlutterSecureKey.withheldBy(Platform.environment), read once at launch; withheld, read() answers null without touching flutter_secure_storage and write() throws a StateError. scripts/perf-app-launch.sh --macos runs each launch as env -u CLAX_APP_DIR CLAX_APP_NO_KEY=1 <copy>/Contents/MacOS/Clax; on Android the variable does not reach the app and a Keystore read asks nothing, as the script's header says. bazelisk test --nocache_test_results //apps/clax_app:platform_secure_key_test //apps/clax_app:daemon_supervisor_test //apps/clax_app:dart_analyze //scripts:perf_app_launch_test: 4 tests pass, among them 'a withheld key reads as none and refuses writes, never reaching the secure storage', 'with the key withheld (CLAX_APP_NO_KEY=1) the daemon starts with no key, and the secure storage is never asked' and '--macos: ... every launch runs without CLAX_APP_DIR and with CLAX_APP_NO_KEY=1' (19 checks). Not yet run against a real build: the first launch of a build that includes 49a0cccabd27 shows whether the keychain question is gone.","supersedes":"344145cc322008054ede5842b4f592c81814881ea5f8f97f1fd1fa152dfe4501","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:55:07.639016Z","id":"a6e08d38ca0ec88f6cae99e64574a1f5f44d158c14826684bf699373d90c7b64","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"b2ec527c930657a3dd5a08a218f3822ec9970d4da107504d6be9c0fa8b05261c","summary":"The macOS baseline no longer waits on record 344145cc: 49a0cccabd27 makes the app read no saved key under CLAX_APP_NO_KEY=1, which scripts/perf-app-launch.sh --macos sets for every launch. docs/usage.md ('Taking the launch baseline') step 1 now names a build C that includes 49a0cccabd27 (checked with git merge-base --is-ancestor) and comes from before 'Run the app on the embedded core'; a build from before 49a0cccabd27 still asks for the keychain.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/app-macos-dev.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:34:12.510892Z","id":"10b19b86e20a58799a5cbc5b35b7cf90ecd9ee0358d988eb05ec19af2e48960b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:49a0cccabd27","summary":"Fixed in 49a0cccabd27: scripts/app-macos-dev.sh runs scripts/patch-pub.sh --i-know-what-i-am-doing after packing the home bundle and runs flutter run with PUB_CACHE=apps/clax_app/build-native/pub-cache. Its dry run lists both; its build steps run for real on 2026-10-20 (patch-pub.sh --i-know-what-i-am-doing, then PUB_CACHE=<that cache> flutter build macos --debug in apps/clax_app) printed 'patch-pub: patched webview_flutter_wkwebview 3.27.0' and '✓ Built build/macos/Build/Products/Debug/Clax.app': the Mac runner compiles against the patched plugin.","supersedes":"67b692abc6583acd375a8de32b532ba314b3c0559b3787b50642692397dd94d4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/patch-pub.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:34:12.578923Z","id":"7d178416d48d2f4a2fa20477d22951ba6775bdf4f0e645abe2b58568ba3c1c37","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:49a0cccabd27","summary":"The acting run ran on 2026-10-20 (through the build steps of scripts/app-macos-dev.sh as of 49a0cccabd27): flutter pub get --enforce-lockfile into apps/clax_app/build-native/pub-cache left pubspec.lock unchanged (git status), the patch applied ('patch-pub: patched webview_flutter_wkwebview 3.27.0'), and flutter build macos --debug with that PUB_CACHE built Clax.app with the runner's SchemeHost.swift, which uses the patched configurationHook.","supersedes":"3d901cf2ba8e71090d93ab5d0c9271d623e6611d0d71097365b936cf824d1b3e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/app-android-emulator.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:34:56.404581Z","id":"781044e3932a1fff5d5e4fc0e0d06078e0f3763668783e250128154f3e067dfc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:49a0cccabd27","summary":"Fixed in 49a0cccabd27: scripts/app-android-emulator.sh's .running file records the serial, the PID, the PID's start time (ps -o lstart) and, once booted, its command (ps -o comm), and --start, --serial and --stop trust the PID only while both still match. bazelisk test //scripts:app_android_emulator_test --nocache_test_results PASSED; its cases 'a reused PID with another start time is neither reported nor stopped' and 'a reused PID with the start time but another command is neither reported nor stopped' fail on the script before 49a0cccabd27.","supersedes":"5abbf5a5856d48ac87240afb0b5c876b5037b0a6838fb2d9c3b208805b878c9f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/app-android-emulator.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:34:56.872883Z","id":"34c7f5c4ca85f8ec9339a1a24a119974e0664ba0a1d6be09bbbc625ef8625775","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:49a0cccabd27","summary":"Fixed in 49a0cccabd27: from the emulator's spawn until it has booted, an EXIT trap (with INT, TERM and HUP turned into exits) stops that emulator by its PID and its adb server on port+10000 and removes the .running file. bazelisk test //scripts:app_android_emulator_test --nocache_test_results PASSED; its cases 'an emulator that exits while booting leaves no adb server and no .running file' and 'an interrupted boot stops the emulator and its adb server' (a SIGTERM to --start during the boot wait) fail on the script before 49a0cccabd27. The Android spike run of 2026-10-20 ended with the emulator's PID gone and nothing listening on 15554.","supersedes":"31561f1121a4b35b580d3d41fdcc408ed33410559201aed58cd8f83e2e11e081","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/app-android-emulator.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:34:57.272922Z","id":"cdfb514dc2b067bd0856ffac47c11b9bd1552fe969dfdcc66d97747cd3e4a8b9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:49a0cccabd27","summary":"Fixed in 49a0cccabd27: --start boots with -read-only, --clean removes target/android-avd and target/android-home (refusing while the emulator runs), and docs/bazel.md says the system image is kept once per user in Bazel's repository contents cache (4.3 GB unpacked, its 1.9 GB zip in the content-addressable cache). After --clean and one run of bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_android_scheme_spike (PASSED in 43.3s), target/android-avd was 32 MB, against 1.4 GB after the run before. //scripts:app_android_emulator_test covers --clean.","supersedes":"c0e0d9f797ba3393cce36adf41e7a06641f838153db0074c7432416b4b1bafd1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/run.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T22:27:54.051708Z","id":"f6ee89f7c9e8e65c63a367b7dd436ae72480b6598505b23ba4a0fbd5c36ebc82","body":{"detail":"scripts/run.sh's native app-test (and scripts/quality_gates.sh's app lane) runs apps/clax_app/tool/check.sh with no CLAX_EMBED_LIB, and the real tests open the core only from it (apps/clax_app/test/support/paths.dart claxEmbedLib, test/core/core_real_test.dart: skip 'CLAX_EMBED_LIB is not set'). Under Bazel they run against //crates/clax-embed:clax_embed_host. A native run therefore reports them skipped, not run.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":283},"end":{"line":286},"content_hash":"a3afb51ff2fd5ea5c819e7bfa8a5ac7c8f3d93c97b068015208a74d2b084cc8f"},"suggested_fix":"Build the host core with cargo build -p clax-embed and pass CLAX_EMBED_LIB=$PWD/target/debug/libclax_embed.dylib (or .so) to tool/check.sh.","summary":"Natively, app-test's flutter test gives the *_real_test.dart files no CLAX_EMBED_LIB, so they skip","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-ios-spawns.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T22:27:54.170348Z","id":"64e542a79d991c07fc507b8604e1fddfa62c50462b764969ee97319a276dc30d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"1661f24fabf51ad340e5ece58d228eb3bfc66bd78d222ee5596115eca2c8ffef","summary":"crates/clax-ios is deleted: the iOS arms now compile in //crates/clax-embed:ios_build_test, which builds clax-embed and its dependencies (clax-server, clax-mcp, clax-core, clax-realtime) for aarch64-apple-ios and aarch64-apple-ios-sim (bazelisk test //crates/clax-embed:ios_build_test: PASSED on 49a0cccabd27's tree), and check-ios-spawns.sh scans clax-embed in clax-ios's place. Whether an allowed function runs nothing on iOS is still reviewed per entry.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-clax.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T22:27:54.170626Z","id":"1b456793b5361f09bfe10dbd25a205c9a81d5d342924df72bf8f3e25b971de04","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"688a1a4ebb8462d93bf00159a978838a27eef14d5b16f26e7a891a1ed0598577","summary":"Still so for the core: the script now builds clax-embed, whose web UI comes from crates/clax-embedded/src/web.rs (RustEmbed over $CLAX_WEB_DIST_DIR, and the workspace's rust-embed in Cargo.toml has no debug-embed feature), so 'scripts/build-app-clax.sh android --debug' places a jniLibs/<abi>/libclax_embed.so that reads web/dist from the build machine. just app-clax-native is gone; the script is run directly. Bazel's //crates/clax-embed:clax_embed_android_* are always optimized.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-clax.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T22:27:54.170878Z","id":"12de43040d222240062ed5b3c6f4158bca0bcda42258635d148f92e90776881a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"87888a6c851e5ee5685c4f01036464e501fb2d73299c977a5885e25f3de84ec2","summary":"The path is now scripts/build-app-clax.sh:61, and the script builds clax-embed; just app-clax-native is gone, so this applies when the script is run directly (or through the -native app recipes).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/app-phone.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T02:46:16.741535Z","id":"041f6310aca663739fddb7038c9f97b22ed9d97ad42f39b13947ff05c7a695be","body":{"detail":"The release app says 'clax-core: ready pid=<pid>', each 'clax-timing: <line>' and 'clax-home: snapshot kept' through debugPrint (lib/core/core_host.dart, lib/platform/timings.dart, lib/home/home_snapshot.dart), which Flutter's engine writes to logcat under the tag flutter; app-phone.sh and perf-app-launch.sh read them with 'adb logcat -d --pid=<pid>'. scripts/test-perf-app-launch.sh drives the Android loop over a fake adb; app-phone.sh has no test. Neither was run on a phone or the emulator, so that a release build's debugPrint reaches logcat, and that the line is there before APP_PHONE_READY_WAIT (300 s) on a first launch after an upgrade, are unverified.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":242},"end":{"line":287},"content_hash":"91087b64b5270ac09f73ecd2b5eb7cb5e5e07cde27e85f39f777b6998a9fd7df"},"suggested_fix":"Install the //apps/clax_app:apk build on the emulator (scripts/app-android-emulator.sh --start), launch it, and check 'adb logcat -d --pid=$(adb shell pidof dev.empathic.clax)' shows clax-core: ready and the clax-timing: home-usable line; then run scripts/perf-app-launch.sh --android --runs 3 --i-know-what-i-am-doing there.","summary":"The logcat readiness wait and perf-app-launch.sh --android's log reading are tested only against a fake adb, not a phone","tags":["android","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-clax.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T02:46:16.741646Z","id":"ecf93b93bd18c26b7e39e268f6e5e4571924514f054c2d1b167f60d867c03716","body":{"detail":"scripts/test-build-app-clax.sh checks the commands a release macos build prints. No native release build was run (agents run no cargo build in a worktree), so the x86_64-apple-darwin build of clax-embed's C dependencies (ring, the bundled SQLite) through cc-rs on an arm64 Mac, and the lipo'd dylib loading in a Release app on each CPU, are unverified. The Bazel Mac app (//apps/clax_app:macos_app) stays arm64 only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":58},"end":{"line":73},"content_hash":"8c2cbc5e7836d5c301c4731ed97c470b13cf2b85fc3a962e03476e1c7838b4ae"},"suggested_fix":"scripts/build-app-clax.sh macos on a Mac with both rustup targets, then lipo -info apps/clax_app/build-native/macos/libclax_embed.dylib (expect x86_64 arm64) and just app-macos-native.","summary":"The universal macOS core (aarch64 and x86_64 joined with lipo) is checked only by the script's dry run, never built","tags":["macos","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/run.test.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:57.162111Z","id":"f4b54e1e9ce4bdb91e2150c8f4250d18f87f175b52d7c6e23b93120668c34c47","body":{"detail":"Failure: on any Linux runner (CI's ubuntu-latest, .github/workflows/ci.yml:9), `stat -f %l FILE` is GNU stat's --file-system mode, where %l is the maximum file name length (255), and it exits 0, so the `|| stat -c %h` fallback never runs. links is \"255\", `[ \"$links\" = 1 ]` is false, and the check \"web: copies, writable, one link each\" fails though run.sh's _copy_dist made single-link copies. CI run 39266520838 on main (2026-10-19) shows exactly this: `FAIL: //scripts:run_choice` with `FAIL: web: copies, writable, one link each` while every other run_choice check passed. GNU's format sequences for -f: https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/html_node/stat-invocation.html. scripts/test-extension-signing.sh:104 and scripts/test-dev.sh:48 order the two the safe way (GNU `-c` first, which BSD stat rejects).","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":228},"end":{"line":228},"content_hash":"72f97b8c6d1d42bf5ac76e214f90e9ed98a8811cd5df603ec9ac0a053dc99ab4"},"suggested_fix":"Try GNU first: `links=\"$(stat -c %h \"$f\" 2>/dev/null || stat -f %l \"$f\")\"` (BSD stat has no -c, so it falls through), or use `find \"$f\" -links 1` which is the same on both.","summary":"The link-count probe tries BSD `stat -f %l` first, which GNU stat accepts as a file-system query, so //scripts:run_choice fails on Linux","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:57.162295Z","id":"8b67a515a0421d516a1342d690291a6fd323926418909f08f26d10cfcb657491","body":{"detail":"When the lock's recorded PID is dead, each waiting run does `rm -rf \"$LOCK\"; continue`. Runs A and B both read the dead PID; A removes the lock, mkdirs a new one and writes its PID; B, still acting on the dead PID it read, then runs `rm -rf \"$LOCK\"`, deleting A's lock, and mkdirs its own. Both now run the gates in one checkout, which the comment at lines 19-21 says corrupts both (one `pnpm install` replaces node_modules under the other's tests). A run killed between `mkdir` (line 23) and `echo $$ > \"$LOCK/pid\"` (line 31) also leaves a lock with no PID, which every later run waits on forever (an empty holder is never treated as stale).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":22},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"9a092ae504f4657e6be4d49017d31998aad7699519204633339d362b82c7034c"},"suggested_fix":"Take over a stale lock by atomically renaming it aside (`mv \"$LOCK\" \"$LOCK.stale.$$\"` succeeds for one run only) and re-read the PID from the moved directory before removing it; or hold the lock with `flock` on a file (util-linux, `brew install flock`) / `shlock` on macOS. Treat a PID-less lock older than a minute as stale.","summary":"Two runs that both find a stale lock can both remove it, so the second deletes the first's fresh lock and both run in one checkout","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:57.162327Z","id":"ad18e90298d2d15379dc6f64ad4dcadc388175aaeda341efba964d6a0639b0e5","body":{"detail":"AGENTS.md (\"Code\") says tests are load-tolerant with no wall-clock budgets in any check. lane_e2e awaits tests-built, linted and release-built (lines 94-96), and lane_pi and lane_binary await clax-built; each await counts 9000 iterations of `sleep 0.2` and then prints \"gave up waiting\" and fails the lane, even though the lane it waits on is still running and will mark it. On a cold cargo cache under load (every lane compiling at once into one target/), the debug test build or the release build can exceed 30 minutes, and the run then fails for time alone. The cap is also unnecessary: `await` already returns when the awaited lane's `.done` file appears without the mark (lines 255-258), so a failed or killed lane cannot leave it waiting forever.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":250},"end":{"line":263},"content_hash":"19fd9a7beed7c7f6152436899aac5ca4205e7398bfc392aa98f9b0d164618c05"},"suggested_fix":"Drop the iteration cap and rely on the `.done` check (a lane always touches `.done` on exit via its EXIT trap, line 243); if a backstop is wanted, wait on the awaited lane's PID being alive instead of a count.","summary":"`await` gives up after 9000 polls (about 30 minutes), a wall-clock budget that fails the run on a cold or loaded machine","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/run.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:57.162369Z","id":"7c6ad22aa8176cb7d53106c9502f00c016fdc89c6e42689834d3a72ba02d309b","body":{"detail":"scripts/bazel-test.sh:208-213 lints every crates/*/clippy.toml crate a second time with its own clippy.toml, and run.sh's lint hard-codes `-//crates/clax-commands/...` and `//crates/clax-commands:clippy.toml`. Today only crates/clax-commands/clippy.toml exists, so they agree; when a second crate gains a clippy.toml, `just lint` lints it with the root clippy.toml only and passes code that `just ci` and CI reject.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"68ec81302306d8391c6b96afbc532139bb3088a67067c3ef6d8bbd1032b600b0"},"suggested_fix":"Build the per-crate passes in run.sh's lint from the same `for toml in crates/*/clippy.toml` loop (excluding each such crate from the first pass), or move the loop into a helper in scripts/lib/ that both scripts call.","summary":"`just lint` under Bazel names clax-commands as the one crate with its own clippy.toml, while scripts/bazel-test.sh finds them by glob","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/bazel-test.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:57.162507Z","id":"6dc3b28382d3fb217b648ef2a261edae83171a36365bedb7fe041bab6ff9ba0b","body":{"detail":"scripts/lib/build-system.sh:44-64 (_bazel_usable) uses a plain `bazel` only when `bazel --version` matches .bazelversion, because \"another version fails far from the cause\". scripts/bazel-test.sh:44 and scripts/bazel-sync.sh:99-102 pick `command -v bazelisk || command -v bazel` with no such check, so `just ci` (run.sh decides Bazel via build-system.sh, then calls bazel-test.sh) and a direct `scripts/bazel-test.sh` can run different binaries, and a mismatched distro bazel gets used by bazel-sync.sh and fails with lockfile or module errors that do not name the version.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":44},"end":{"line":49},"content_hash":"7995342c044599561bc20d21a46bf36b338bd50773ebf7f310e9002cd11893ab"},"suggested_fix":"Source scripts/lib/build-system.sh in bazel-test.sh and bazel-sync.sh and use `_bazel_usable`/$BAZEL (keeping BAZEL_SYNC_BAZEL as the test override), so all three pick Bazel the same way.","summary":"bazel-test.sh and bazel-sync.sh take any `bazel` on PATH, where scripts/lib/build-system.sh accepts a plain bazel only at the .bazelversion version","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/bazel-test.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:00:47.488664Z","id":"df06584b5b7b1721b482eb43bea38fe2c67654bc5268cb2c663c0b37be493664","body":{"detail":"scripts/lib/build-system.sh:52-60 uses a plain bazel only when `bazel --version` equals .bazelversion. scripts/bazel-test.sh:44 is `bazel=\"$(command -v bazelisk || command -v bazel || true)\"` and scripts/bazel-sync.sh:99-102 the same (after BAZEL_SYNC_BAZEL), with no version check. With Bazelisk installed both pick it, so through `just ci` they agree; a direct `scripts/bazel-test.sh` or `just bazel-sync` with only a mismatched distro bazel uses it where run.sh would fall back to native. Suggestion kind fits.","kind":"comment","references":"6dc3b28382d3fb217b648ef2a261edae83171a36365bedb7fe041bab6ff9ba0b","summary":"confirmed: bazel-test.sh and bazel-sync.sh accept any bazel on PATH; build-system.sh checks the version","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/run.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:00:47.488851Z","id":"f3957a64f75a8ea05da271892c776986d2fc68a7ebce3e85ed81a61563a35f4f","body":{"detail":"scripts/run.sh:146-150 excludes `-//crates/clax-commands/...` and passes `//crates/clax-commands:clippy.toml` by name; scripts/bazel-test.sh:208-213 loops `for toml in crates/*/clippy.toml`. `ls crates/*/clippy.toml` prints only crates/clax-commands/clippy.toml, so they agree today and diverge when a second crate adds one.","kind":"comment","references":"7c6ad22aa8176cb7d53106c9502f00c016fdc89c6e42689834d3a72ba02d309b","summary":"confirmed: run.sh lint hard-codes clax-commands while bazel-test.sh globs crates/*/clippy.toml","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:00:47.489009Z","id":"eb0eba83e0c9500edb558999b6e9c3f52e688959ee8b5a7f60157ff80328517f","body":{"detail":"scripts/quality_gates.sh:23-31: `while ! mkdir \"$LOCK\"; do holder=$(cat \"$LOCK/pid\" ...); if [ -n \"$holder\" ] && ! kill -0 \"$holder\"; then rm -rf \"$LOCK\"; continue; fi; ... sleep 10; done; echo $$ > \"$LOCK/pid\"`. Two waiters that both read the same dead PID can each `rm -rf \"$LOCK\"`, the second removing the lock the first just re-created. A run killed between `mkdir` and `echo $$ > \"$LOCK/pid\"` leaves an empty holder, which the `[ -n \"$holder\" ]` guard never treats as stale.","kind":"comment","references":"8b67a515a0421d516a1342d690291a6fd323926418909f08f26d10cfcb657491","summary":"confirmed: stale-lock takeover races, and a PID-less lock is waited on forever","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:00:47.489323Z","id":"ccdb0be6921c2d1c6a7cf8612c6d6c71af98ca57d96f12574b68fbc0d36746f7","body":{"detail":"scripts/quality_gates.sh:252-263: `i=$((i + 1)); if [ \"$i\" -gt 9000 ]; then echo \"quality gates: gave up waiting for $1\"; return 1; fi; sleep 0.2`, and the comment above says \"or after 30 minutes\". The `.done` check at lines 256-258 already ends the wait when the awaited lane exits without marking (the lane's EXIT trap touches `.done`, line 243). AGENTS.md (\"Code\"): \"no wall-clock budgets in any check\".","kind":"comment","references":"ad18e90298d2d15379dc6f64ad4dcadc388175aaeda341efba964d6a0639b0e5","summary":"confirmed: await fails after 9000 x 0.2 s, a wall-clock budget AGENTS.md forbids","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/run.test.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:00:47.489785Z","id":"ee0f8f66a597af389b055ff5502aa3951cda5b7b0cb0401555c6aba8bfa529ae","body":{"detail":"scripts/run.test.sh:228 `links=\"$(stat -f %l \"$f\" 2>/dev/null || stat -c %h \"$f\")\"`; GNU stat -f is file-system mode where %l is max filename length (https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/html_node/stat-invocation.html). scripts/BUILD.bazel:224-226 defines run_choice; .github/workflows/ci.yml:9 runs-on ubuntu-latest and :43 runs scripts/bazel-test.sh --ci. `gh run view 39266520838 --log-failed | grep FAIL` prints `FAIL: //scripts:run_choice (Exit 1)` and `FAIL: web: copies, writable, one link each`. scripts/test-extension-signing.sh:104 and scripts/test-dev.sh:48 put GNU `-c` first.","kind":"comment","references":"f4b54e1e9ce4bdb91e2150c8f4250d18f87f175b52d7c6e23b93120668c34c47","summary":"confirmed: `stat -f %l` first makes //scripts:run_choice fail on Linux CI","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/run.test.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:57:10.385698Z","id":"de9fe1caf67cdf0d2e219686adb0b0caa6984d38fb9927a397e56c4501b0604b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:42c6250d3","summary":"Fixed: link count uses find -links 1; bazelisk test //scripts:run_choice passes; verified in ubuntu:24.04 that find -links 1 works where stat -f %l misreads.","supersedes":"f4b54e1e9ce4bdb91e2150c8f4250d18f87f175b52d7c6e23b93120668c34c47","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:57:10.536795Z","id":"ab6736a7310639f15714f6be907f1e0035078749a8fb9881300b0053ea9aefd4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2bf60a87e","summary":"Fixed: the checkout lock is a flock(2) (scripts/lib/checkout-lock.sh), atomic with no stale takeover; bazelisk test //scripts:checkout_lock passes (kill -9 release, six contenders never overlap).","supersedes":"8b67a515a0421d516a1342d690291a6fd323926418909f08f26d10cfcb657491","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:57:10.928581Z","id":"cbd0e15f3ee046447c184f34def84757d35474577b910da7ae0d9b2beeaaf4b6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c3844a30c","summary":"Fixed: the 9000-poll limit in await is removed; await returns when the lane's .done appears.","supersedes":"ad18e90298d2d15379dc6f64ad4dcadc388175aaeda341efba964d6a0639b0e5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/bazel-test.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:57:12.096629Z","id":"7f001ead11be38da4b50f435297d159f95c88726f141a57533a8c34d6d7d4451","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:cdd021d8f","summary":"Fixed: bazel-test.sh and bazel-sync.sh pick Bazel through scripts/lib/build-system.sh _bazel_usable; scripts/bazel-sync.test.sh wrong-version case passes.","supersedes":"6dc3b28382d3fb217b648ef2a261edae83171a36365bedb7fe041bab6ff9ba0b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/run.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:57:12.371419Z","id":"1996cf5cfa6104a28ddcf20527339ee3fdbf8ceab72597f3a6e1f098faab4ed6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e5668ae1c","summary":"Fixed: run.sh finds crates/*/clippy.toml by glob; bazelisk test //scripts:run_choice case 'lint: each crate's own clippy.toml, found by glob' passes (failed before).","supersedes":"7c6ad22aa8176cb7d53106c9502f00c016fdc89c6e42689834d3a72ba02d309b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:37:25.205789Z","id":"bec0532206b6cefb87b9eb93687ab6ec947a0fbeb45b6cdc5b8e421f78570079","body":{"detail":"is_signed_commit and is_signed_tag look for a gpgsig header or a SIGNATURE block. git verify-commit/verify-tag would need gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile for SSH signing, which the owner's config may not set, so the presence check is what keeps an unsigned commit or tag from being pushed. A signature by the wrong key would pass.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":123},"end":{"line":124},"content_hash":"5730bf23787f48c7ab971a356cfae8c05e7cbcd85b8cac921374d6a7f4e69eaf"},"suggested_fix":"Verify with git verify-commit/verify-tag when gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile (or a GPG keyring) is configured, and fall back to the presence check otherwise.","summary":"Signature checks before a push test that a signature is present, not that it verifies","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:37:25.205875Z","id":"6dde1fb4be9fc559ca154216904cadf2d67a0e411d8b702f679a45fb584c29b8","body":{"detail":"The waits poll gh run view every CLAX_RELEASE_POLL_SECONDS, at most CLAX_RELEASE_MAX_POLLS times, instead of gh run watch: gh run watch has no timeout of its own (macOS has no timeout(1)), and the poll interval can be zero in scripts/test-release-script.sh. gh run watch would show job-level progress.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":350},"end":{"line":380},"content_hash":"678a9a096111d177ba44699b939a54c0e4fda1670f12a2db635ea8d1bfecb377"},"summary":"gh run watch for the workflow waits","tags":["revisit:the owner wants job-level progress during the waits","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:37:25.205914Z","id":"a6d9af55fa2a3989f5847ef21c00a9fbe6776f1f39453d66ac7c885110e6a9d6","body":{"detail":"gh workflow run prints no run ID. A dispatch by someone else of publish-pi.yml in the same seconds could be taken for this one; a crash between the dispatch and writing target/release/X.Y.Z/publish-pi-run makes the next run dispatch again, which .github/workflows/publish-pi.yml refuses once npm has the version. Accepted: publish-pi is dispatched by hand, by the owner, rarely.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":433},"end":{"line":451},"content_hash":"c9f62387e471280a97633263891a099d277aac441e43bb08727924c87a1973c8"},"summary":"The Publish Pi package run is identified as the first new workflow_dispatch run on main after the dispatch","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:37:25.205945Z","id":"85c0f890b0094da2c8887b85ce193b9b3716723c20eac285f04d1c0e5d80ceb3","body":{"detail":"Resuming after a failed just ci, a fix made in the work tree is committed with git commit -S -a in the release (or pin) commit, as the manual procedure's git commit -am did. step_5 and step_11 list the files they commit. A fix committed separately would make main ahead of origin/main by a commit that is not the release's, which preflight refuses.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":252},"end":{"line":262},"content_hash":"7d89c57ec7f706cacfcc8efdcb68f043c5dbfd7a5f4684e9c8bf4cdb24a02913"},"summary":"While steps 2-4 or 9-10 are pending, every modified tracked file goes into the release or pin commit","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/test-release-script.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:37:25.205989Z","id":"1f155a8a31c6a922f139f5b355378d711b54c77ad288004baf1a20e29cf79f96","body":{"detail":"find_run, publish_runs, run_state and release_has_sums in scripts/release.sh pass --json/--jq to gh; the fake ignores both and prints the filtered text. A wrong field name or jq expression would pass this test and fail against GitHub.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":60},"end":{"line":104},"content_hash":"aa1f9ab4aae7b49e6282d91e45165a2048cb8c978db5466342ac6a95767c74b9"},"suggested_fix":"Have the fake print JSON and run the --jq expression through jq (or gh's own --jq on a fixture) where jq is installed.","summary":"The fake gh prints what each --jq expression would, so release.sh's jq expressions are not tested","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:45:14.254504Z","id":"611746e6000ad3582b610c2856982c49d1409555390ffac66a64fb1f611e7936","body":{"detail":"Failure: a release of the version already exists from an earlier push of the tag (built from another commit), the tag is re-made on a new \"Release X.Y.Z\" commit and pushed by steps 6-7. done_8 (release_has_sums) is true at once, so step 8 never looks at the Release run on the new commit, which fails with \"a release with the same tag name already exists\" (gh release create in .github/workflows/release.yml, job publish). Step 9 then pins the old release's SHA256SUMS: the plugins download binaries built from a commit the tag no longer names, and the script reports \"Clax X.Y.Z is released.\" Reproduced with scripts/test-release-script.sh's fakes: with the release already listing SHA256SUMS and run 101 set to \"completed failure\", the run prints \"Step 8: Wait for the Release workflow: done already\", never calls gh run view 101, and exits 0. Real precedent: empathic/clax run 39267463465 (v0.5.0 re-pushed on 85c30382b) failed in \"Publish v0.5.0\" with that message while the release still holds assets uploaded 2026-10-18 from run 39141786735 on 48d8487a2.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":322},"end":{"line":322},"content_hash":"1e8ac0b436320484471cf721c8afdcd0df32df7fb2313b3eb4778440c7a7de4c"},"suggested_fix":"Make done_8 require the newest Release run on REL_COMMIT (find_run release.yml push) to have concluded success as well as SHA256SUMS on the release; when the run failed and the release exists, stop and say the release must be deleted (gh release delete) before the run is rerun.","summary":"Step 8 counts as done whenever a release vX.Y.Z lists SHA256SUMS, without looking at this tag's Release run","tags":["review","review:release-script","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:45:14.254586Z","id":"a6b7d2185ce871757033b30841516a409904d4b3114ddc596c4221df68b1349d","body":{"detail":"Failure: any commit pushed to origin's main between step 12 and step 14 (the CI wait in step 13 can take up to an hour; other work lands on main often) makes `gh workflow run publish-pi.yml --ref main` publish @empathic/clax-pi from that later commit, which CI has not passed, while docs/usage.md:573 says the package is published from the pin commit. Nothing between steps 12 and 14 compares origin/main with PIN_COMMIT. Reproduced with scripts/test-release-script.sh's fakes and a gh wrapper that pushes a commit to the bare origin while run 201 is viewed: the dispatch happened with origin's main at the foreign commit, not the pin commit, and the run ended \"Clax 0.6.0 is released.\"","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":440},"end":{"line":452},"content_hash":"6e37914dd56af00eb1bca4c92cf9d6d2b7e2aeccd1e294a35a476af64654a869"},"suggested_fix":"Before dispatching, fetch origin main and refuse unless it equals PIN_COMMIT (saying how to publish by hand from the pin commit); or dispatch on a ref that names the pin commit, e.g. a short-lived branch, if publish-pi.yml is to accept one.","summary":"publish-pi is dispatched on main's tip, which need not be the pin commit CI was waited on","tags":["review","review:release-script","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:45:14.254629Z","id":"05ebb5a79af9341d13ea7c2f319e19655849165933a4b2fdac3f501383c97ab1","body":{"detail":"Failure: step 13 fails (CI on the pin commit fails or the wait gives up) or step 14 fails, and a commit lands on origin's main before the rerun (for example the fix for that CI failure). The rerun refuses in preflight with \"0.6.0 is not newer than the tag v0.6.0, a release finished or taken over by later commits on main\", so the Pi package is never published by the script. Reproduced with scripts/test-release-script.sh's fakes: run 201 \"completed failure\", a commit pushed to origin, `git pull --ff-only`, rerun: exit 1 with that FAIL line. docs/usage.md:545-546 calls this state a finished release.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":214},"end":{"line":226},"content_hash":"7409b5ca5eac519651186678d1b5facf8082c03ebae1f40975d9e9b1653d23ca"},"suggested_fix":"Once the pin commit is an ancestor of origin/main and the tag is on the release commit, let the run resume steps 13-14 (they need no clean or current checkout), or name the manual commands for the remaining steps in the refusal.","summary":"A release whose CI wait or Pi publish has not finished cannot be resumed once main moves past the pin commit","tags":["review","review:release-script","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:45:14.254665Z","id":"7c263195ba65197adaa7e52e0092b8e817aa5bb080f10d983043a90399e8044f","body":{"detail":"Failure: steps 7-8 take tens of minutes; a commit pushed to origin's main meanwhile makes step 12's push fail (non-fast-forward; correctly not forced). Every recovery is then refused: the rerun says \"main is 1 commit(s) behind origin/main (git pull --ff-only)\"; git pull --ff-only cannot fast-forward the diverged main; a merge gives \"the checkout has a commit origin/main lacks that is not this release's: \\\"Merge branch 'main' ...\\\"\"; a rebase rewrites the release commit, so the pushed tag no longer tags it and preflight refuses \"the tag v0.6.0 exists on origin and does not tag a \\\"Release 0.6.0\\\" commit\". Reproduced with scripts/test-release-script.sh's fakes and a gh wrapper that pushes a commit to the bare origin while run 101 is viewed (first two refusals observed; the rebase case follows from check_version at scripts/release.sh:218-221).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":419},"end":{"line":426},"content_hash":"e2201218d3542543b8e8b0d905dde86da65e23693be535e7faaa75d3eb6b7f1d"},"suggested_fix":"Accept a merge of origin/main into the checkout after the release commit (the tag stays on the release commit, and the pin commit goes on top), or rebase only the pin commit onto origin/main with the release commit merged; and say in the step 12 failure what to do.","summary":"A push of main rejected because origin's main moved during the Release wait leaves no way to resume","tags":["review","review:release-script","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:45:14.254699Z","id":"896b25693d4ba1b5eff78c5ebf8128526bdfad492f1f402837a878569c7b6089","body":{"detail":"Failure: a \"Release 0.6.0\" commit reached main earlier and was reverted (or abandoned and followed by other work), with no v0.6.0 tag. Preflight passes; commit_with_subject finds the old commit, so done_3, done_4 and done_5 (scripts/release.sh:317-319) are true: bazel-sync, just ci and the release commit are skipped, step 6 tags and step 7 pushes the old, reverted commit, and the bump from step 2 lands in the pin commit. Reproduced with scripts/test-release-script.sh's fakes (signed \"Release 0.6.0\" commit, git revert, push): steps 3-5 printed \"done already\", origin's v0.6.0 tagged the reverted commit, exit 0 \"Clax 0.6.0 is released.\"","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":112},"end":{"line":114},"content_hash":"442990c5230e55647b7fd0b3fc2df85cc09371e11d4efaf52affc619c0fb2552"},"suggested_fix":"Take as the release commit only one in origin/main..HEAD, or the commit origin's or the local tag already names; refuse a \"Release X.Y.Z\" commit already on origin/main without the tag.","summary":"The release commit is looked up in the whole history, so an old \"Release X.Y.Z\" commit already on main is tagged and steps 3-5 skipped","tags":["review","review:release-script","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:45:14.254803Z","id":"ccc2298ee1c620bf1166b76ec8d8d32ed3235799378427b53969906739c44345","body":{"detail":"await_output returns 1 as soon as the polled command fails (`out=\"$(\"$@\")\" || return 1`), and with pipefail find_run fails whenever gh run list does, so one transient API or network error ends step 8 or 13 with \"no Release workflow run on vX.Y.Z appeared\" or \"no CI run on <sha> appeared\", which misnames the cause. await_run likewise stops at the first failed run_state. The run is resumable, so the cost is a restart and a misleading message.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":337},"end":{"line":346},"content_hash":"f6bf464770b49d84c697b062680c276a8eba6aed63cd276533030d126a0065fc"},"suggested_fix":"Count a failed poll as an empty one (retry until MAX_POLLS), and say \"gh run list failed\" with gh's error when the last poll failed.","summary":"One failed gh call ends a wait of up to 90 minutes, reported as the run not appearing","tags":["review","review:release-script","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:47:33.574931Z","id":"3afb6ebd1bdd078da7edcdbfb0e9567b5ec6ba943aa61643eccdd7214bdad14f","body":{"detail":"scripts/release.sh:322 is `done_8() { release_has_sums; }`; release_has_sums (125-127) only greps `gh release view $TAG` assets. Reproduced with scripts/test-release-script.sh's harness (lines 1-196) and the fakes: new_case; `: > $FAKE_STATE/published`; `echo 'completed failure' > $FAKE_STATE/101`; act -> rc=0, output \"Step 8: Wait for the Release workflow: done already\" and \"Clax 0.6.0 is released.\", `gh run view 101` called 0 times. Precedent checked read-only: `gh run view 39267463465 --repo empathic/clax` is a failure on headSha 85c30382b, log-failed \"Publish v0.5.0 ... a release with the same tag name already exists: v0.5.0\"; `gh release view v0.5.0` assets were created 2026-10-18T15:59:30Z. Kind concern is right.","kind":"comment","references":"611746e6000ad3582b610c2856982c49d1409555390ffac66a64fb1f611e7936","summary":"confirmed: step 8 counts as done from the release's SHA256SUMS alone, never looking at this tag's Release run","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:47:33.575119Z","id":"36a409b3e43c29a36fac4887c358a54d4482ce679b8f404525004cd98e3be266","body":{"detail":"scripts/release.sh:446 runs `gh workflow run publish-pi.yml --ref main -f dry_run=false`; step_13 (427-432) and step_14 (440-452) never compare origin/main with PIN_COMMIT, and refresh (138-145) does not fetch. .github/workflows/publish-pi.yml:43 is a bare `actions/checkout@v4`, which checks out the dispatched ref's tip at dispatch time. docs/usage.md:573 says the package \"is published from the pin commit\". A commit landing on main during step 13's wait (up to MAX_POLLS*POLL = 90 minutes, line 58) is what gets published. Kind concern is right.","kind":"comment","references":"a6b7d2185ce871757033b30841516a409904d4b3114ddc596c4221df68b1349d","summary":"confirmed: publish-pi is dispatched on main's tip with no check that it is still the pin commit","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:47:33.575277Z","id":"cfccaf0dfb38c30d2f42ee28f8b431ad2a9e9193ecbffab9cc77cd6e6b8b76df","body":{"detail":"scripts/release.sh:222-225 refuse whenever the tag exists, REL_COMMIT is an ancestor of origin/main, and PIN_COMMIT is not origin/main's tip. Reproduced with scripts/test-release-script.sh's harness: new_case; `echo 'completed failure' > $FAKE_STATE/201`; act -> rc=1 \"release.sh: step 13 (Wait for CI on main) failed.\"; push an empty commit to the bare origin from another clone; `git pull --ff-only origin main`; set 201 to success; act -> rc=1 \"FAIL: 0.6.0 is not newer than the tag v0.6.0, a release finished or taken over by later commits on main\". The Pi package was never dispatched. Kind concern is right.","kind":"comment","references":"05ebb5a79af9341d13ea7c2f319e19655849165933a4b2fdac3f501383c97ab1","summary":"confirmed: once main moves past the pin commit, a rerun after a failed step 13 or 14 is refused as a finished release","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:47:33.575432Z","id":"56aa1c3e46fc0868e2062663804f7eb328bf6e5814f1d6678be7099c36a6218c","body":{"detail":"Reproduced with scripts/test-release-script.sh's harness and a gh wrapper earlier on PATH that pushes an empty commit to the bare origin from another clone on the first `gh run view 101`: act -> rc=1, \"! [rejected] main -> main (fetch first)\", \"release.sh: step 12 (Push main) failed.\"; rerun -> rc=1 \"FAIL: main is 1 commit(s) behind origin/main (git pull --ff-only)\" (scripts/release.sh:237-238); `git pull --ff-only` -> \"Diverging branches can't be fast-forwarded\"; after `git merge origin/main`, rerun -> rc=1 \"FAIL: the checkout has a commit origin/main lacks that is not this release's: \\\"Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main'\\\"\" (241-249). A rebase rewrites the release commit, which scripts/release.sh:220-221 then refuse against origin's tag. Kind concern is right.","kind":"comment","references":"7c263195ba65197adaa7e52e0092b8e817aa5bb080f10d983043a90399e8044f","summary":"confirmed: a push of main rejected because origin moved during the Release wait has no accepted recovery","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:47:33.575595Z","id":"76822c3f3487f731809b05436484baa9f399d46de867c7ecc8bd72706c5034d2","body":{"detail":"scripts/release.sh:112-114 search all of HEAD's history; done_3..done_5 (317-319) only test REL_COMMIT non-empty. Reproduced with scripts/test-release-script.sh's harness: new_case; set CLAX_VERSION 0.6.0, `git commit -S -a -m 'Release 0.6.0'` (c4553f2), `git revert --no-edit HEAD`, push; act -> rc=0, \"Step 3/4/5: ... done already\", step 6 tags and step 7 pushes; origin's refs/tags/v0.6.0^{commit} = c4553f2780ee (the reverted commit); origin main: Pin the plugins to Clax 0.6.0 / Revert \"Release 0.6.0\" / Release 0.6.0; \"Clax 0.6.0 is released.\" just ci ran only for step 10, bazel-sync not at all. Kind concern is right.","kind":"comment","references":"896b25693d4ba1b5eff78c5ebf8128526bdfad492f1f402837a878569c7b6089","summary":"confirmed: an old reverted \"Release X.Y.Z\" commit on main is taken as the release commit and tagged","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:47:33.575905Z","id":"2ba0fbd7c4e48743c7de36eb986d246f5f4ed1c02a2a0ef907a672120acc1fec","body":{"detail":"scripts/release.sh:340 `out=\"$(\"$@\")\" || return 1`; line 54 sets pipefail, so find_run (129-133) returns gh's failure status. step_8 (406-407) and step_13 (430) then say \"no Release workflow run on $TAG appeared\" / \"no CI run on $PIN_COMMIT appeared\"; await_run (354) stops at the first failed run_state. gh's own stderr is not redirected, so its message is printed above the misleading one. The run is resumable, so suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"ccc2298ee1c620bf1166b76ec8d8d32ed3235799378427b53969906739c44345","summary":"confirmed: one failed gh poll ends the wait and is reported as no run appearing","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:46:30.529773Z","id":"ae96713e49cf6a1b7f18ab22931616e7aad91f7d8cca5a0567c656c9b725a688","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f88ecf8fe","summary":"Step 8 is done only when the release lists SHA256SUMS and a successful Release run on the tag built the tag commit's tree (release_of_tree, trees read through gh api); a release no such run built is refused before the pin, saying to delete it and rerun. Evidence: bazelisk test //scripts:release_script PASSED at 0d25dd1f7; its cases 'a release built from another tree stops before the pin, saying to delete it', 'a release no successful run built from this tree is never pinned' and 'a release built from the tag's tree by an earlier run, as after re-signing, is accepted' pass.","supersedes":"611746e6000ad3582b610c2856982c49d1409555390ffac66a64fb1f611e7936","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:46:30.555980Z","id":"1c5d8617b49f9d79479656f9fbe0199f820813b0de8a259dc31fc5939b789d80","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:44516ae8a","summary":"publish-pi.yml takes a sha input (checked to be on main with CI passed) and titles its run after it; release.sh dispatches it with the pin commit (or the merge on it) and finds the run by that title. Evidence: //scripts:release_script PASSED at 0d25dd1f7, case 'the Pi package is published from the pin commit after main moves on' (origin's main moved past the pin during the CI wait; the dispatch carried sha=<pin>).","supersedes":"a6b7d2185ce871757033b30841516a409904d4b3114ddc596c4221df68b1349d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:46:30.581662Z","id":"971cbf9426e44f4612c928e57663afdfbd40c882ba0d98d54b635978066cf750","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:67e4e6ddb","summary":"The release commit is the tag's commit once a tag exists, and before that only a \"Release X.Y.Z\" commit in origin/main..HEAD; one already on origin/main with no tag is refused. Evidence: //scripts:release_script PASSED at 0d25dd1f7, case 'preflight refuses an old \"Release 0.6.0\" commit on origin/main with no tag and changes nothing' (the reverted-commit reproduction).","supersedes":"896b25693d4ba1b5eff78c5ebf8128526bdfad492f1f402837a878569c7b6089","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:46:30.607392Z","id":"b50f99eb13fa9d5cafdc594cb81e7c50a4d8621cba7cb7b7958aa6ff10a58c32","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a51dd211e","summary":"The finished-release refusal is gone; a release is known by its tag and pin commit, so a pulled checkout resumes steps 13-14 after main moves on. Evidence: //scripts:release_script PASSED at 0d25dd1f7, cases 'failed CI on the pin commit stops at step 13, before the publish', 'once main has moved past the pin commit, the next run resumes at the CI wait and publishes from the pin' and 'a finished release with main moved on reports every step done'.","supersedes":"05ebb5a79af9341d13ea7c2f319e19655849165933a4b2fdac3f501383c97ab1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:46:30.633634Z","id":"150579f7a6d65b4f347432ca8066255de2444ef3e1332b75d794c28020cf4356","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ec97a6cb3","summary":"Step 12 merges origin/main on top of the pin commit with a signed merge commit when main has moved on, keeping the tag on the release commit; preflight accepts a checkout behind origin/main while its release commit waits to be pushed. Evidence: //scripts:release_script PASSED at 0d25dd1f7, cases 'main moving during the Release wait is merged on top of the pin commit, signed, keeping the tag', 'a refused push of main stops at step 12 with the pin commit made' and 'after main moved on, the next run merges it on top of the pin commit and finishes'.","supersedes":"7c263195ba65197adaa7e52e0092b8e817aa5bb080f10d983043a90399e8044f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:46:30.687261Z","id":"ed590ca02ad987fe8d25c5cfa431f3fdce0c51dc7f4dab4988f508f953ade1ca","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2ac21ea08","summary":"A failed gh poll counts as an empty one; five failures in a row end the wait with gh's own error, and a wait out of polls says when its last gh call failed. Evidence: //scripts:release_script PASSED at 0d25dd1f7, cases 'a wait rides out gh failing twice' and 'gh failing on every poll stops the wait, naming gh's error'.","supersedes":"ccc2298ee1c620bf1166b76ec8d8d32ed3235799378427b53969906739c44345","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:46:30.713390Z","id":"f4c76ee151c8601844dfe44b24b57889749c36de841b015ea74707608fe27cd8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:44516ae8a","summary":"Obsolete: step 14 now finds the Publish Pi package run by the title publish-pi.yml gives it (\"Publish Pi package <sha>\") and is done once npm has the version; nothing is kept in target/release/X.Y.Z/publish-pi-run.","supersedes":"a6d9af55fa2a3989f5847ef21c00a9fbe6776f1f39453d66ac7c885110e6a9d6","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:46:30.739148Z","id":"11f19198fe8399124ff781e9470718de11eb6e36d5c8c1c1adc8a334f0236ffc","body":{"detail":"is_signed_commit and is_signed_tag look for a gpgsig header or a SIGNATURE block. git verify-commit/verify-tag would need gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile for SSH signing, which the owner's config may not set, so the presence check is what keeps an unsigned commit or tag from being pushed. A signature by the wrong key would pass.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":138},"end":{"line":139},"content_hash":"5730bf23787f48c7ab971a356cfae8c05e7cbcd85b8cac921374d6a7f4e69eaf"},"suggested_fix":"Verify with git verify-commit/verify-tag when gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile (or a GPG keyring) is configured, and fall back to the presence check otherwise.","summary":"Signature checks before a push test that a signature is present, not that it verifies","supersedes":"bec0532206b6cefb87b9eb93687ab6ec947a0fbeb45b6cdc5b8e421f78570079","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:46:30.764547Z","id":"5f0470905b7e14f1222f8ee7d1a707b9c01bd6b4540383a5453362ca429535ec","body":{"detail":"Resuming after a failed just ci, a fix made in the work tree is committed with git commit -S -a in the release (or pin) commit, as the manual procedure's git commit -am did. step_5 and step_11 list the files they commit. A fix committed separately would make main ahead of origin/main by a commit that is not the release's, which preflight refuses.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":342},"end":{"line":352},"content_hash":"7d89c57ec7f706cacfcc8efdcb68f043c5dbfd7a5f4684e9c8bf4cdb24a02913"},"summary":"While steps 2-4 or 9-10 are pending, every modified tracked file goes into the release or pin commit","supersedes":"85c0f890b0094da2c8887b85ce193b9b3716723c20eac285f04d1c0e5d80ceb3","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:46:30.790863Z","id":"f89237a048e0a5472dadc9c63d237e126e5612001a28837106f85e31a8f5fde0","body":{"detail":"The waits poll gh run view every CLAX_RELEASE_POLL_SECONDS, at most CLAX_RELEASE_MAX_POLLS times, instead of gh run watch: gh run watch has no timeout of its own (macOS has no timeout(1)), and the poll interval can be zero in scripts/test-release-script.sh. gh run watch would show job-level progress.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":496},"end":{"line":543},"content_hash":"5e82e2f546bef04ed9414a9ab0e7522467dacf89427ec3b404ccd7c523a4f603"},"summary":"gh run watch for the workflow waits","supersedes":"6dde1fb4be9fc559ca154216904cadf2d67a0e411d8b702f679a45fb584c29b8","tags":["revisit:the owner wants job-level progress during the waits","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/test-release-script.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:46:30.817593Z","id":"2c23047a0c95d2f96616f76b9eb1e0c4f1c46ea9d230f390cbcd038c7f2663d3","body":{"detail":"find_run, publish_run, run_state, release_has_sums and release_of_tree in scripts/release.sh, and scripts/release-exists-check.sh (tested in scripts/test-release.sh), pass --json/--jq to gh; the fakes ignore both and print the filtered text. A wrong field name or jq expression would pass the tests and fail against GitHub. The expressions were checked by hand with jq on sample JSON.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":73},"end":{"line":177},"content_hash":"2bb1bbd2c5033f13146c31eae11d1b7b07a716014f63043be87ae145621d289d"},"suggested_fix":"Have the fakes print JSON and run the --jq expression through jq where jq is installed.","summary":"The fake gh prints what each --jq expression would, so release.sh's jq expressions are not tested","supersedes":"1f155a8a31c6a922f139f5b355378d711b54c77ad288004baf1a20e29cf79f96","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:46:30.844829Z","id":"e9adde2f969721195800b70f0168a165c62a0bef8f1cbfc2e387025872f29ad7","body":{"detail":"When origin's main moves before step 12, release.sh merges origin/main on top of the pin commit with a signed merge commit. Rebasing only the pin commit onto origin/main would keep main linear, but the release commit is not on origin/main yet at that point, so the rebase would have to carry it too, rewriting the commit the pushed tag names; the merge keeps the tag valid. CI and the Pi package then run on the merge commit.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":596},"end":{"line":621},"content_hash":"6806331a7512381a5fc87aeea1d05f803e59d9c5a1b393aa11ddeb36f59d800d"},"summary":"Rebasing the pin commit onto origin/main when main moves during a release","tags":["revisit:the release commit reaches main before the tag is pushed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:46:30.844848Z","id":"b354b3cf516e6954c2cc126df8165b4de0edfb9d38c4e3a887ee18aea25d444e","body":{"detail":"pi_first_publish typechecks the package as publish-pi.yml does: pnpm install --frozen-lockfile and pnpm run typecheck in a git worktree of the pin commit under target/release/X.Y.Z/pi-publish, removed afterwards. It runs once, on the owner's machine, before the npm package exists; later releases publish through the workflow.","kind":"waiver","summary":"The first Pi publish installs plugins/pi's dependencies in a temporary worktree under target/release/","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release-exists-check.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:03:55.565986Z","id":"577547928c53388ef09df230b2d0bfbec85ebafa27d1d19eea845ef9f389e02f","body":{"detail":"Failure: run 1 on vX.Y.Z builds tree A and makes the release; the release is deleted and the tag moved to a commit with tree B (the recovery scripts/release.sh:190-195 and this script's own error message prescribe: delete the release, rerun); run 2 builds and publishes tree B. A later push of the tag to a re-signed copy of the tree-B commit fails here (earliest = run 1, tree A), and a push of the tag back to a tree-A commit prints skip=true while the release holds tree B's files. `gh run list --branch <tag>` keeps runs from before the tag moved, and `sort_by(.createdAt) | .[0]` picks run 1. scripts/release.sh:177-187 (release_of_tree) uses a third rule, any successful run with the tree, so the two disagree in the same scenario, while docs/usage.md:650 says release.sh judges the release 'the same way'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":30},"end":{"line":48},"content_hash":"9700d58722f91050624f43b0d49bf125e49cb2bd89a5dda2c021480dc370bd8f"},"suggested_fix":"Judge by the run that made the current release: the newest successful run whose publish job ran (not skipped), or the newest successful run created before the release's createdAt (gh release view --json createdAt). Use the same rule in release.sh's release_of_tree, and keep docs/usage.md:642-652 in step.","summary":"The skip compares against the earliest successful Release run on the tag, not the run that made the release that exists now","tags":["review","review:release-script-2","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:03:55.566121Z","id":"a5db835d064ea3a31bc894e1a0759e0d877588b1d7d234d90a4c254fce6e0d78","body":{"detail":"Failure: the merge of origin/main conflicts; the person follows the printed `git merge -S origin/main -m ...`, resolves, and runs `git commit` (or `git merge --continue`) as told. git does not carry -S over a conflict stop, so without commit.gpgsign=true the merge commit is unsigned (checked: a conflicted `git merge -S` then `git commit --no-edit` in a scratch repository with gpg.format=ssh yields a commit with no gpgsig header). The rerun's step 12 then says '<sha> carries no signature; not pushing main' (scripts/release.sh:612-614) and stops. docs/usage.md:553-555 gives the same instruction.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":604},"end":{"line":609},"content_hash":"5ed11263fca07d74f8dace586a80f8e6a34295f5319b147b6fdfc64ece789ab3"},"suggested_fix":"Say 'resolve, then git commit -S' (or `git -c commit.gpgsign=true merge --continue`) in the printed message and in docs/usage.md:555.","summary":"The hand-merge instructions produce an unsigned merge, which step 12 then refuses to push with no remedy given","tags":["review","review:release-script-2","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:03:55.566163Z","id":"c428bca5d2461b46ed07587a89f3777adfc695c23e146afa25519e7459026456","body":{"detail":"Failure: `npm publish` succeeds, then the await on npm listing the version runs out of polls or the person interrupts the run; target/release/X.Y.Z/pi-first-publish is never written. The rerun finds step 14 done (done_14 is pi_has_version) and step 15 checks the marker (scripts/release.sh:723), so the trusted-publisher setup and README switch are never printed, and the next release's publish-pi.yml run fails at npm's OIDC exchange.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":671},"end":{"line":681},"content_hash":"6766d6b509426b543d291239aafd46fd5ac81159a3752d82f0ae10139f8c38d2"},"suggested_fix":"Write the marker as soon as npm publish exits 0 (before the await), or have step 15 decide from npm (the package has exactly one version) rather than a local file.","summary":"The first-publish marker is written only after npm lists the version, so a publish that succeeded can lose the trusted-publisher reminder","tags":["review","review:release-script-2","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/test-release-script.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:03:55.566213Z","id":"5c5b1bd3618a83e850f491197127fd5ea6dd7cdb93d1a6f12c0a09ce1985fe58","body":{"detail":"Failure: a case with several checks (e.g. case_23, five refusals) hits an unbound variable under set -u after its first PASS; the subshell exits, its result file has one PASS and no FAIL, and the gate passes. `wait` is called without PIDs, so no status is collected.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":761},"end":{"line":772},"content_hash":"05f9c5b453acf3235470609328d7f5c6e342f0d267b86df150cc568dfbc53205"},"suggested_fix":"Record each background PID and `wait \"$pid\"` per case, failing on a non-zero status, or end every case with a sentinel line the collector requires.","summary":"The parallel runner ignores each case's exit status, so a case that dies after its first PASS hides its later checks","tags":["review","review:release-script-2","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release-exists-check.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:05:39.188736Z","id":"2e949076807430015c982df7d631c917219c3e35491de8f0c6bb2fff839d1847","body":{"detail":"scripts/release-exists-check.sh:30-31 lists successful release.yml push runs on --branch \"$tag\" with no filter on the run's commit or the release's creation time and takes `sort_by(.createdAt) | .[0]`, so a run that built a since-deleted release still decides. scripts/release.sh:181-185 (release_of_tree) instead returns 0 when any of up to 50 successful runs on the tag built the tag commit's tree. docs/usage.md:646-650 describes the earliest-run rule and says release.sh judges 'the same way'. The rules disagree once a tag has successful runs on two trees. Kind concern is right: this needs a deleted release and a moved tag.","kind":"comment","references":"577547928c53388ef09df230b2d0bfbec85ebafa27d1d19eea845ef9f389e02f","summary":"confirmed: the skip judges by the earliest successful run on the tag, and release.sh judges by any successful run","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:05:39.189194Z","id":"2371c685706222c28c57294c4095f1fd3a5517731f4a10e56eaf340ae57c0ecb","body":{"detail":"Reproduced with git 2.50.1 in a scratch repository (GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null, gpg.format=ssh, user.signingkey set to a fresh ed25519 key): `git merge -S -m M o` stops on a conflict; after resolving, `git commit --no-edit` makes a two-parent commit 'M' and `git cat-file commit HEAD | grep -c gpgsig` prints 0, while `git commit -S --allow-empty` in the same repository prints 1. scripts/release.sh:606-608 tells the person to 'resolve, commit'; :612-613 then stops on '<sha> carries no signature'. docs/usage.md:554-555 gives the same instruction.","kind":"comment","references":"a5db835d064ea3a31bc894e1a0759e0d877588b1d7d234d90a4c254fce6e0d78","summary":"confirmed: a conflicted git merge -S finished with git commit makes an unsigned merge commit, which step 12 then refuses","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:05:39.189342Z","id":"6bc51f7b9d08ec4413bd95637905c20c210df356eb40b70aa23e88ae1ad0a17d","body":{"detail":"scripts/release.sh:672-677 writes target/release/$V/pi-first-publish only when pi_publish_from returns 0, and pi_publish_from returns 1 when the await at :697-698 gives up after `npm publish` (:695) succeeded. done_14 is pi_has_version (:451), so a rerun skips step 14, and step_15 prints the trusted-publisher and README lines only when the marker exists (:723-729).","kind":"comment","references":"c428bca5d2461b46ed07587a89f3777adfc695c23e146afa25519e7459026456","summary":"confirmed: the marker depends on the post-publish await, while step 14 counts as done once npm lists the version","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/test-release-script.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:05:39.189491Z","id":"3ae0502721c656efcf902248b90b672a36fd84cedaf561074dbddd9986b1c1e3","body":{"detail":"scripts/test-release-script.sh:24 sets `set -uo pipefail`, so an unbound variable ends a case's subshell. :763-768 starts each case with `(\"$c\") > \"$T/result.$c\" 2>&1 &` and calls `wait` with no PIDs, which collects no status. :769-773 fails only on a FAIL line or on no PASS/FAIL line at all, so a result file holding one PASS and nothing after it is counted as passing.","kind":"comment","references":"5c5b1bd3618a83e850f491197127fd5ea6dd7cdb93d1a6f12c0a09ce1985fe58","summary":"confirmed: case exit statuses are discarded, so a case that dies after one PASS passes the gate","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release-exists-check.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:21:06.165415Z","id":"17199fecb2f8efa52899e5d6ab5dd1fa5b2664631e972a47b7e8778216fd5dee","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:80b271f94","summary":"The Release workflow writes a SOURCE_TREE asset (covered by SHA256SUMS); release-exists-check.sh --tree reads it, or for an older release the tree of the newest successful Release run on the tag created before the release, the run that uploaded it; the workflow's skip and release.sh's step 8 (release_tree) both use that one script. Evidence: bash scripts/test-release.sh passes its release-exists-check cases (SOURCE_TREE decides over the runs; no SOURCE_TREE judged by the uploading run; neither places it) and //scripts:release PASSED at 4fde7462c; //scripts:release_script cases 'a release with no SOURCE_TREE is judged by the run that uploaded it' and 'a release no rule can place is never pinned' pass.","supersedes":"577547928c53388ef09df230b2d0bfbec85ebafa27d1d19eea845ef9f389e02f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:21:06.190765Z","id":"b6f60df4c13bd98abafc6b16e520d3f8cc36860e1cf874c54af3c486637e3910","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:14c9d717e","summary":"The conflict message and docs/usage.md say to commit the resolved merge with git commit -S; step 12's refusal of an unsigned newest commit says to sign it with git commit --amend -S --no-edit. Evidence: //scripts:release_script PASSED at 4fde7462c, cases 'an unsigned hand-made merge is not pushed, and the refusal says how to sign it' and 'once signed as told, the next run pushes the merge and finishes'.","supersedes":"a5db835d064ea3a31bc894e1a0759e0d877588b1d7d234d90a4c254fce6e0d78","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:21:06.216230Z","id":"7e34ce095a0f95962266c4f40e975e5fc7073fd3d8a7957db2d16ff3efad0578","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:895671b8f","summary":"The first-publish marker is written as soon as npm publish succeeds, before the wait for npm to list the version. Evidence: //scripts:release_script PASSED at 4fde7462c, cases 'a first publish npm has not listed yet stops step 14, keeping the publish recorded' and 'the rerun finds the publish done and prints the trusted-publisher setup'.","supersedes":"c428bca5d2461b46ed07587a89f3777adfc695c23e146afa25519e7459026456","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/test-release-script.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:21:06.241737Z","id":"a9586fdbe99f2af77c175b7f9f9e1149cfe481e9aee8af6baf59319adcaa6fd3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:cdcc5c6b3","summary":"Each case's subshell is waited for by its PID and must exit 0, which it does only after its last check; a nonzero status fails the gate. Evidence: a standalone copy of the runner logic under /bin/bash reports status 0 for a passing case and 1 for one that dies on an unbound variable after its first PASS; //scripts:release_script PASSED at 4fde7462c.","supersedes":"5c5b1bd3618a83e850f491197127fd5ea6dd7cdb93d1a6f12c0a09ce1985fe58","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:21:06.293930Z","id":"f6de1c8ed65493a324c8e6117b687050dfc44723201c7258fb0c8a766d89ef1b","body":{"detail":"is_signed_commit and is_signed_tag look for a gpgsig header or a SIGNATURE block. git verify-commit/verify-tag would need gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile for SSH signing, which the owner's config may not set, so the presence check is what keeps an unsigned commit or tag from being pushed. A signature by the wrong key would pass.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":144},"end":{"line":145},"content_hash":"5730bf23787f48c7ab971a356cfae8c05e7cbcd85b8cac921374d6a7f4e69eaf"},"suggested_fix":"Verify with git verify-commit/verify-tag when gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile (or a GPG keyring) is configured, and fall back to the presence check otherwise.","summary":"Signature checks before a push test that a signature is present, not that it verifies","supersedes":"11f19198fe8399124ff781e9470718de11eb6e36d5c8c1c1adc8a334f0236ffc","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:21:06.319962Z","id":"433aa864e6818945ed863334f3c191d8d5214223add3b5ef0bc3662b724a713d","body":{"detail":"Resuming after a failed just ci, a fix made in the work tree is committed with git commit -S -a in the release (or pin) commit, as the manual procedure's git commit -am did. step_5 and step_11 list the files they commit. A fix committed separately would make main ahead of origin/main by a commit that is not the release's, which preflight refuses.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":351},"end":{"line":361},"content_hash":"7d89c57ec7f706cacfcc8efdcb68f043c5dbfd7a5f4684e9c8bf4cdb24a02913"},"summary":"While steps 2-4 or 9-10 are pending, every modified tracked file goes into the release or pin commit","supersedes":"5f0470905b7e14f1222f8ee7d1a707b9c01bd6b4540383a5453362ca429535ec","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:21:06.345571Z","id":"472dec706a3bcc304b079acc757622f70c2b4b9b7d4f0dadbd11bdf5bf8d1a63","body":{"detail":"The waits poll gh run view every CLAX_RELEASE_POLL_SECONDS, at most CLAX_RELEASE_MAX_POLLS times, instead of gh run watch: gh run watch has no timeout of its own (macOS has no timeout(1)), and the poll interval can be zero in scripts/test-release-script.sh. gh run watch would show job-level progress.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":520},"end":{"line":583},"content_hash":"d91f04e05c222ed3bdf13a9b181a70f38a7998538825a6710589c2abaf881dde"},"summary":"gh run watch for the workflow waits","supersedes":"f89237a048e0a5472dadc9c63d237e126e5612001a28837106f85e31a8f5fde0","tags":["revisit:the owner wants job-level progress during the waits","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:21:06.371312Z","id":"23265a9b545122925eb6788d041569eb15566612863158ea6cf119324baddc45","body":{"detail":"When origin's main moves before step 12, release.sh merges origin/main on top of the pin commit with a signed merge commit. Rebasing only the pin commit onto origin/main would keep main linear, but the release commit is not on origin/main yet at that point, so the rebase would have to carry it too, rewriting the commit the pushed tag names; the merge keeps the tag valid. CI and the Pi package then run on the merge commit.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":636},"end":{"line":669},"content_hash":"0806723e951751dabba86dd175876588b20eafb6fb9865a1aa3c61d37fc8f10e"},"summary":"Rebasing the pin commit onto origin/main when main moves during a release","supersedes":"e9adde2f969721195800b70f0168a165c62a0bef8f1cbfc2e387025872f29ad7","tags":["revisit:the release commit reaches main before the tag is pushed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/test-release-script.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:21:06.396991Z","id":"c8ce4bd1c86fa7816ab3234f6eef4b15022cfa46239a1befb79b8ebd384e5618","body":{"detail":"find_run, publish_run, run_state, ci_gate_state, release_has_sums and the npm-environment checks in scripts/release.sh, and scripts/release-exists-check.sh (tested in scripts/test-release.sh), pass --json/--jq to gh; the fakes ignore both and print the filtered text. A wrong field name or jq expression would pass the tests and fail against GitHub. The expressions were checked by hand with jq on sample JSON.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":76},"end":{"line":211},"content_hash":"08fce10606c1e2c6cbb716068ef72a5dfe0b9dadfece02629fa33dfe71fc1640"},"suggested_fix":"Have the fakes print JSON and run the --jq expression through jq where jq is installed.","summary":"The fake gh prints what each --jq expression would, so release.sh's jq expressions are not tested","supersedes":"2c23047a0c95d2f96616f76b9eb1e0c4f1c46ea9d230f390cbcd038c7f2663d3","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T03:54:19.864687Z","id":"97789c4e780b3aa538ad961df7a7cbbdb4d98b6931f78e70c9a6640b79046209","body":{"detail":"learn_weights averages each step's '== step N ran Ss' lines from every target/release/*.log. A step resumed part-way (step 8 or 13 finding its workflow run already finished, step 4 after a cached just ci) records a few seconds and pulls that step's estimate far below its typical duration, so the overview and the percentages read optimistic after a resumed release; logs also accumulate across versions with no cap. A median, or ignoring runs under some fraction of the typical duration, would resist this.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":163},"end":{"line":178},"content_hash":"cd9c2a36a6cbc22bafe30dfa7aa326e60dd0291d2a27c98b45955d2616ac20bc"},"suggested_fix":"Use the median per step, or the newest few full runs only.","summary":"Learned step durations average every recorded run, including resumed steps that took seconds","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/vendor-rquickjs-sys.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T01:31:52.386340Z","id":"0d86ca0c6d2908140132788844d2b49053efed3a7aa8ede8581a74ac90710382","body":{"detail":"third_party/rquickjs-sys is rquickjs-sys 0.14.0 with third_party/rquickjs-sys.patch (interrupt every 100 steps, uncatchable out-of-memory, Function constructors that refuse a body closing the function; docs/bazel.md, \"Patched third-party crates\"). scripts/vendor-rquickjs-sys.sh --check downloads the crate to compare, so neither the Bazel tests nor CI run it, and an edit made to the copy alone would go unnoticed. Moving rquickjs to a new version also means reapplying the patch to a new QuickJS by hand. An offline check (the copy against a pinned digest of its own files) would close the first part.","kind":"concern","summary":"The patched rquickjs-sys copy is checked against its patch only by hand: --check needs the network and no gate runs it","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/crate-package.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T01:31:52.386365Z","id":"0f55a69b16a4bcb1c1a82776d7f556a136581287d103b83be5b7006469e77c3b","body":{"detail":"Cargo.toml's [patch.crates-io] points rquickjs-sys at third_party/rquickjs-sys, and crates.io ignores [patch] in a published package. A clax built from crates.io would get QuickJS polling its interrupt handler every 10,000 steps, a catchable out-of-memory error (QuickJS can abort() rejecting an async function with the null it throws when even that error cannot be allocated) and Function constructors that run a body that closes the function. scripts/crate-package.py bundles workspace crates as modules; it would need to bundle the patched sys crate too (its C sources and build script), or the published binary must not include ClaxBot's native sandbox. No crate that clax-cli depends on uses clax-bot-js yet.","kind":"concern","summary":"The crates.io package cannot carry the [patch.crates-io] of rquickjs-sys: once clax-cli depends on clax-bot-js, `cargo install clax` builds unpatched QuickJS","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/vendor-rquickjs-sys.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:03:17.629692Z","id":"ae84639c0c74c5cf8a7c3b7bf7f2d6dfcb6e80c3cc7eaeaafdfd22a94b46986a","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"The script is now scripts/vendor-rquickjs.sh (754cbe26); the concern is recorded again there","supersedes":"0d86ca0c6d2908140132788844d2b49053efed3a7aa8ede8581a74ac90710382","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/vendor-rquickjs.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:03:17.659468Z","id":"967bd31279e7fc6e3bd1e9f62d756d502db32ae01f4aac06616a7fbca6f68c37","body":{"detail":"third_party/clax-rquickjs-sys (rquickjs-sys 0.14.0 with third_party/rquickjs-sys.patch) and third_party/clax-rquickjs-core (rquickjs-core 0.14.0 over it) are written by scripts/vendor-rquickjs.sh, whose --check downloads both crates to compare, so neither the Bazel tests nor CI run it and an edit made to a copy alone would go unnoticed (QuickJs::self_test still refuses an engine that lost the patch's three guarantees). Moving rquickjs to a new version means reapplying the patch to a new QuickJS by hand. An offline check (the copies against a pinned digest of their own files) would close the first part.","kind":"concern","summary":"The patched QuickJS crates are checked against their sources only by hand: --check needs the network and no gate runs it","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/crate-package.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:03:17.659893Z","id":"065de6fc518862ec1e549169fdb0c9075bcf740c0ded644cee6a031d68ca6046","body":{"detail":"The patched QuickJS is built as two workspace crates with names of their own (third_party/clax-rquickjs-sys, third_party/clax-rquickjs-core; docs/bazel.md, Patched third-party crates), marked publish = false, and there is no [patch] any more. A crates.io package cannot depend on unpublished path crates, so once clax-cli reaches clax-bot-js (through clax-server), scripts/crate-package.py stops: it runs scripts/check-crate-layers.py --publishable, which fails while clax-cli reaches a third_party/ crate or the workspace has a [patch] (scripts/test-check-crate-layers.sh tests both). Releasing then needs the owner to publish the two crates (as they are, MIT, from scripts/vendor-rquickjs.sh), turn their publish = false off, and make crate-package depend on them by version rather than bundle them; or to ship the crates.io binary without ClaxBot's native sandbox. Which, and when, is the owner's call; nothing has been published.","kind":"concern","summary":"A crates.io `clax` that includes ClaxBot first needs the owner to publish clax-rquickjs-sys and clax-rquickjs-core","supersedes":"0f55a69b16a4bcb1c1a82776d7f556a136581287d103b83be5b7006469e77c3b","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/crate-package.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:14:44.514024Z","id":"16c29222f0c95cc7c1fe94cc5b562cd68d02030452b40a40976f6a807343a195","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"065de6fc518862ec1e549169fdb0c9075bcf740c0ded644cee6a031d68ca6046","summary":"Since git:e3a49468 the package builds without them: clax-bot-js is an optional dependency of clax-server behind its default native-sandbox feature, crate-package.py and check-crate-layers.py --publishable leave optional dependencies out with their features (bundled sources read the feature as any()), so the published clax answers every ClaxBot script 'unavailable' (clax_server::bot::UnavailableSandbox). `python3 scripts/check-crate-layers.py --publishable .` prints 'clax-cli is publishable'. A crates.io clax with a working sandbox still needs the owner to publish the two crates, which is this record's question.","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-crate-layers.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.329464Z","id":"2fb9726be59d07802ff4eaaba1bef9d6a725106359c72dcae5d1d6455120620d","body":{"detail":"The layout's picture (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-workspace-layout-design.md section 2.1, lines 184-188) and ALLOWED here gain the crates the hosted work added: clax-rt (the runtime seam, tokio natively and a Worker's event loop on wasm32) depends on no workspace crate and every daemon crate uses it, so it joins clax-core's set; clax-git depends on nothing; clax-content-git on clax-core, clax-rt and clax-git. crates/clax-worker stays outside the workspace. This amends the decided layout spec, which is the owner's.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":41},"end":{"line":61},"content_hash":"f693cb114b700e1ad0dda12cc65103081f43aed34876df43188016d531ce265f"},"summary":"Place clax-rt beside clax-core, clax-git on its own and clax-content-git over both in the layout","supersedes":"904f8fe2617a660a7b40d8ce6a99608d286b2a72ba8c9ba0409327bf9486ffff","tags":["layout","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/crate-package.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.356747Z","id":"b53bd589bacd49c96f643e1d4879e9852fb60d71516b966a1f6fa5a1213a01f6","body":{"detail":"Not taken: it makes about eleven internal crates (clax-core, clax-store, clax-server, ...) public crates.io names that others can depend on, each release has to publish them in layer order with versioned path dependencies, and clax-embedded would still need its web UI, extension and plugins copied inside its own directory at publish time. The generated package keeps every internal crate private at the cost of rewriting paths (rewrite_sources, lines 240-263).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2},"end":{"line":43},"content_hash":"1f457dd9dc8444086e6472273d57ca5f18fcac98d7fd93fe3a73a070837c365f"},"summary":"Publish every workspace crate to crates.io instead of one generated clax package","supersedes":"54f2cebff7455dc8dd70dfaefffba283d87f7ff21b1166c392264ac987cb2e35","tags":["revisit:a workspace crate is wanted as a library on crates.io, or the path rewrite in scripts/crate-package.py breaks on a source pattern it cannot handle","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/crate-package.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.385512Z","id":"da1375a6e1d55495ecc3365a25b08d53908df9c9261f0f995162cde93fd8b949","body":{"detail":"rewrite_sources replaces every crate:: in a bundled library crate's sources with crate::<module>:: and every clax_<name>:: with crate::clax_<name>::, comments and string literals included. True of the sources at this commit (git grep finds none of these patterns in the eleven bundled crates' src/). A #[macro_export] macro would move to the package root and break its crate::<module>:: callers; a crate feature would be dropped (merged_dependencies refuses optional dependencies); a string such as a serde 'with = \"crate::x\"' is rewritten, which is right, but a log or error message quoting a path would change. tracing targets already read clax::clax_server::... in the package instead of clax_server::... . just crate-package (cargo check --locked of the packed crate) catches whatever does not compile.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":240},"end":{"line":263},"content_hash":"60a7470fdeceb23fa40696d9dd071b492298c652ad77d652836201163f9e7bbe"},"summary":"The package's module rewrite is textual and assumes the bundled crates have no #[macro_export] macros, no extern crate, no crate features and no strings naming crate paths","supersedes":"24303270533236998727e5f7ca681eed8273d90551f9ca9be3237987f3c06117","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/crate-package.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:51:06.332442Z","id":"e2118ee1f88ca176f1fd003354a46efc38537330c3026bb43e12dac1112b7b72","body":{"detail":"merged_dependencies (scripts/crate-package.py:121-140) no longer refuses an optional dependency: it leaves it out, dropped_features (lines 98-118) names every feature that turns one on, and rewrite_sources (line 469-470) replaces each such feature = \"<name>\" in the bundled sources with any(). The concern's 'no crate features' and 'merged_dependencies refuses optional dependencies' now hold only for features that turn on no optional dependency, which are still dropped silently; the rest of the concern (crate:: rewrite in comments and strings, #[macro_export], extern crate) stands. The owner may revise the root's summary.","kind":"comment","references":"da1375a6e1d55495ecc3365a25b08d53908df9c9261f0f995162cde93fd8b949","span":{"start":{"line":240},"end":{"line":263},"content_hash":"60a7470fdeceb23fa40696d9dd071b492298c652ad77d652836201163f9e7bbe"},"summary":"Since this branch the rewrite handles one kind of crate feature: an optional dependency's features are dropped and read as any()","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-daemon.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:18.692892Z","id":"8484768980cb8b9fdc744d05462d058fb274a8de4ef9b776bd97ff6448e45188","body":{"detail":"It does not run the loads together, does not cover several viewers, asset uploads, MCP wait_for_feedback, the sweepers or clax doctor (none of which stalled cheap requests when measured by hand). Besides the gallery and inbox requests alone (lines 27-33), it judges no request slower than its probes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":6},"end":{"line":18},"content_hash":"ad06c541e6d3ec8a6ca271624c3ef13fb4fc81521c0b0739dca0566eb14ef4b9"},"summary":"The daemon latency gate runs its loads one at a time, for one viewer, on loopback","supersedes":"0e2a613c3ef1c9aba31ede4949eb53dd6451ecdc786b6fd67212f9d846807dda","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-wasm.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:19.546377Z","id":"96fd42c286b7235e9af5dda0c42d0f390b7c71fb9579069e061e1ab48769271f","body":{"detail":".github/workflows/ci.yml and rust-toolchain.toml add the wasm32-unknown-unknown target, and the script now also tries Debian and Ubuntu's /usr/lib/llvm-<N>/bin. Whether ubuntu-latest has a clang there that targets wasm32 beside an llvm-ar was not checked; the first CI run of the gates shows it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":30},"end":{"line":42},"content_hash":"886063acdb63514f5e66fac3a4df959dd833b2b526af67dc5f1fbfb9531503d9"},"summary":"The wasm32 lane has run on macOS only: CI's Ubuntu LLVM is unverified","supersedes":"93e0f83d91a850717ad4f58f21482ec4ec4b9bbc14fdb94652f95d2c10285326","tags":["gates","ci","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/verify-harnesses.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T04:18:26.717496Z","id":"b97e576293ed718b47538d200c25058d73be5de9fc9e2596556bda045da8afc6","body":{"detail":"Each command runs in a process group of its own (os.setpgid(0, 0) in watchdog), which is a background group on the terminal; a harness that opens /dev/tty and reads it is stopped, then killed at VERIFY_TIMEOUT and reported as '(timeout after Ns)'. (Moved with the code from scripts/verify-harnesses.sh, record dab8712c.)","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":118},"end":{"line":171},"content_hash":"f1525c14a1cb4b64ae0bbe4275b7669a0db8c4e347d366b6a6582a25aa12b46e"},"summary":"A CLI that reads /dev/tty is stopped by SIGTTIN and reported as a timeout","tags":["session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/verify-harnesses.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T04:18:26.718188Z","id":"43a70be7d82404bd5a7ca93df318d2d18d2f1b90f4976a863c55b3660f328e58","body":{"detail":"os.setpgid(0, 0) runs in the child after fork; a signal in the microseconds before it can make the stop handler signal a process group that does not exist yet and wait for the command. (Moved with the code from scripts/verify-harnesses.sh, record c22e9737.)","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":157},"end":{"line":160},"content_hash":"2dacc21a9b6b605bde21e550869654a8cc869fad3cc0f9282318b5e7248c8bc3"},"suggested_fix":"Also call os.setpgid(pid, pid) in the parent after fork.","summary":"The watchdog sets the process group only in the child","tags":["session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-ios-spawns.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T04:18:26.718349Z","id":"68e1cf39cf6a08def07d2ead2982e20e47ed773dd5d86f734dbad44908fa25fa","body":{"detail":"scripts/ios-spawns.allow names a file and function per launch (crates/clax-core/src/gitctx.rs spawn, remote.rs process_started, clax-mcp channel.rs process_argv, tools.rs run_opener, clax-realtime push.rs run_queue); a new launch added to one of those functions, or a gate removed from one, passes. Whether the iOS arms compile is the job of a build of the daemon for aarch64-apple-ios (cargo check --target aarch64-apple-ios -p clax-server -p clax-mcp passes at 49a0cccabd27); whether they run nothing is reviewed per entry. (Moved with the code from scripts/check-ios-spawns.sh, record 1661f24f.)","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":78},"end":{"line":79},"content_hash":"f5852b401bbef578c06513891e453624bfdc33f7b0ad7ff89362f10591b9b08c"},"summary":"An allowed launch is trusted by its function name: the check does not read the cfg that keeps it off on iOS","tags":["revisit:a launch reaches iOS through an allowed function","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
