{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/cloudflare-setup.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:19:38.530871Z","id":"94ed1091a425116a0ae59a2e9803b7691c46f2f8fb2476fd3bc868f9a841953e","body":{"detail":"They were checked once by running a copy of the script under a scratch root whose deploy.mjs and smoke-remote.mjs print their arguments: --production wrote PRODUCTION=1 to setup.env and later runs passed --production; --ci read no setup.env and passed only the given flags; --ci --smoke without CLAX_SMOKE_TOKEN failed before deploying; with it the smoke ran once with no --diag deploys. No test in scripts/ runs the script.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":144},"end":{"line":153},"content_hash":"48e440b5a996581a391cbab277153a1f2588e0f3eef04e28cd120f7df22ba4ae"},"summary":"cloudflare-setup.sh's --ci, PRODUCTION=1 and agent-token smoke paths have no automated test","tags":["untested","deploy","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/setup-prod-github.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:17:34.252628Z","id":"1130687cf48204cdbdb0e8ab657fd671e0d3879c9b3b5bffcfc5d36c5d0c50a6","body":{"detail":"scripts/test-setup-prod-github.sh checks the calls and bodies the script makes, not that GitHub accepts them. Unverified against GitHub: actor_id 5 with actor_type RepositoryRole as the admin role, integration_id 15368 as GitHub Actions on each required check, allowed_merge_methods on the pull_request rule, and the rulesets list's includes_parents query. The first --i-know-what-i-am-doing run is the check: read the ruleset back (gh api repos/empathic/clax/rulesets/<ID>) and compare with docs/prod.md, 'One-time GitHub setup'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":155},"end":{"line":174},"content_hash":"c8e79e0eea6c19c00257e6bfa1b34787c76d5517e60e2081159ec89566fda49e"},"summary":"The ruleset body is tested only against a fake gh, never against GitHub's API","tags":["untested","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:29:16.587479Z","id":"7c2bfdc576b8a3c40cc75af0c2c8e688831daed972d9fc0b789faaa3b86bb656","body":{"detail":"step_18 cherry-picks the \"Release X.Y.Z\" commit, whose diff is scripts/bump-version.sh's output against release/X.Y.Z's merge of origin/main (step 3). A workspace crate, version file or skill tool block that main gains between that merge and the cut is not in that diff, so after the carry main's versions can disagree and scripts/check-version.sh (and CI on main) fails until a follow-up commit runs bump-version.sh there. The cherry-pick applies cleanly in that case, so step 18 does not stop. No case in scripts/test-release-script.sh covers it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":971},"end":{"line":1010},"content_hash":"c88ee769950159e698e7b67dadc43a8cea326aa2f8a76cd6fc6d620602309860"},"suggested_fix":"After the cherry-picks, run scripts/check-version.sh in the carry worktree and stop before the push of main when it fails, saying to run scripts/bump-version.sh X.Y.Z there and amend the release copy, signed.","summary":"The carry cherry-picks the bump onto main's tip, so a crate added on main after the release branch's merge keeps the old version in Cargo.lock","tags":["untested","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:29:16.587939Z","id":"4577bf3f64d5f5525eeaf46d2c8e49b6fbfcee85eb535a94052a1671ef22a346","body":{"detail":"pr_state reads `gh pr list --head release/X.Y.Z --base prod --state all --limit 1 --json state,url`; scripts/test-release-script.sh's fake prints \"OPEN <url>\" or \"MERGED <url>\" from $FAKE_STATE/pr, as the --jq filter would. GitHub's states (OPEN, CLOSED, MERGED), the newest-first order --limit 1 relies on, and gh pr create printing the URL on stdout (step_9) are not exercised against GitHub; a closed, unmerged pull request makes step 9 open a new one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":334},"end":{"line":337},"content_hash":"390117b30b942d20a278ad4b5ee8ddd99061cf65296e1f9489c3297bfee530b9"},"summary":"The pull request's state comes from gh pr list's JSON, which the test's fake gh only imitates","tags":["untested","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:29:16.588186Z","id":"618c00bd461a629f5bdcbf76f5b3cd1ebe5d93b2dc3c9f3cf673fcc3ea129263","body":{"detail":"check_version refuses a cut when origin/prod has no \"Release X.Y.Z\" commit main lacks (case_22b in scripts/test-release-script.sh, a squashed merge), since step 18 cherry-picks that commit to main. docs/usage.md (\"Releasing\") tells the owner to use Create a merge commit. Whether prod's ruleset (docs/prod.md) should allow only merge commits, so a squash cannot happen, is the owner's call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":509},"end":{"line":520},"content_hash":"2fd5756c7e2f6d49a3265e046207a2ab5a672fabbdee8760415cb672164f83a8"},"summary":"The cut needs the release's pull request merged with a merge commit; prod's ruleset does not enforce that","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:29:16.589548Z","id":"0d8a441bba7fc9687ffaeb1f0e920479c8269adb2beb60840aec383534f7f309","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"23265a9b545122925eb6788d041569eb15566612863158ea6cf119324baddc45","summary":"The merge of origin/main on top of the pin commit this alternative was weighed against is gone: main refuses merge commits, and step 18 of scripts/release.sh now cherry-picks the release and pin commits onto origin/main's tip, the tag staying on prod. Proposed for close as obsolete.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:29:16.590025Z","id":"b770aabf654718be126bce8eccbc352f20f5576beafae631c8b6fe7407e8b76f","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"433aa864e6818945ed863334f3c191d8d5214223add3b5ef0bc3662b724a713d","summary":"Renumbered: the steps whose changes go into a commit are now 4-6 (the release commit, on release/X.Y.Z) and 14-15 (the pin commit, on prod), in check_clean in scripts/release.sh; the accepted risk is unchanged.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:34:54.877610Z","id":"bb68d76b8a6f3a31a7289f4913b91793c92b13cd9520df7d471694c641c7078d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:246a0a5d3","summary":"step_18 now runs scripts/check-version.sh in the carry worktree after the cherry-picks and, when the versions disagree, stops before the push of main (main untouched), naming the files and how to bump and amend by hand. Evidence: case_11b in scripts/test-release-script.sh (main gains plugins/new/VERSION after step 3's merge) passes, and //scripts:release_script PASSED under bazelisk at 246a0a5d3; with the check replaced by `if false`, case_11b's two checks fail (rc=0, main pushed with the stale version).","supersedes":"7c2bfdc576b8a3c40cc75af0c2c8e688831daed972d9fc0b789faaa3b86bb656","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:34:54.981114Z","id":"dc29ba7545efefac95f5a93d0958c5429cbc83b6eb8a5c8f66703670fcf60740","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Decided: prod's ruleset allows merge commits only. scripts/setup-prod-github.sh (branch akesling/prod-ci at 7c491568f, line 168) sets the pull_request rule's allowed_merge_methods to [\"merge\"], so a release pull request cannot be squashed; release.sh's refusal stays as the check for a prod set up otherwise.","supersedes":"618c00bd461a629f5bdcbf76f5b3cd1ebe5d93b2dc3c9f3cf673fcc3ea129263","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/setup-prod-github.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:41:56.977054Z","id":"891f8d683984aaadb35c989c4214cd4d614c1bc1cb847ad8cbf3f9db1fa13c4b","body":{"detail":"The ruleset's pull_request rule asks for required_approving_review_count 0, and its bypass actor is the repository admin role (actor_id 5, RepositoryRole), not one person. `gh api repos/empathic/clax/collaborators` lists two admins and several write and maintain collaborators. A writer can open a pull request into prod that raises the version and also edits .github/workflows/deploy-prod.yml; once bazel, worker and version pass, the writer can merge it, and the push runs that workflow in the production environment (deploy-prod.yml:33), whose branch policy admits prod and nothing else. The design (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-prod-releases-design.md, \"GitHub setup\") names only the owner as the one who merges and bypasses. The environment also has no required reviewers, so nothing else stands in the way.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":160},"end":{"line":171},"content_hash":"bf4a597bddc659fb17b1a2621422513a7271264140397699e3ca159daf0600cf"},"suggested_fix":"Require an approval from the owner (required_approving_review_count 1 with a CODEOWNERS rule on everything, or require_last_push_approval), make the bypass actor the owner's account or a team with only the owner, and/or add the owner as a required reviewer on the production environment.","summary":"Anyone with write access can merge into prod, and any repository admin can push to it, which deploys their code with the production secrets","tags":["review","review:prod-releases","security","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/setup-prod-github.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T19:57:31.908895Z","id":"41d95046e65157ea19a63b860a5a93b2f026c45772961d8a9a98e81bd34837c2","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"891f8d683984aaadb35c989c4214cd4d614c1bc1cb847ad8cbf3f9db1fa13c4b","summary":"Confirmed: the ruleset (scripts/setup-prod-github.sh:162-171) asks for required_approving_review_count 0 and has no rule restricting who updates prod, and its bypass actor is the admin role (actor_id 5, RepositoryRole). `gh api repos/empathic/clax/collaborators --jq '.[].role_name' | sort | uniq -c` prints 2 admin, 3 maintain, 1 read, 2 write: four non-admin accounts can merge a pull request into prod once its checks pass.","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/setup-prod-github.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T20:08:32.720100Z","id":"978ac10c308ec0cf23abef2ac838d14be0d84b826f29da69bd1696985b5887ac","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:335c73303","summary":"Decided and fixed. Owner chose: only the owner may get code into prod. The prod ruleset (scripts/setup-prod-github.sh step 2) gains GitHub's 'Restrict updates' rule (type update, update_allows_fetch_and_merge false; https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/configuring-branches-and-merges-in-your-repository/managing-rulesets/available-rules-for-rulesets#restrict-updates): only the bypass actors, the admin role with bypass_mode always, update prod, so writers and maintainers open pull requests but cannot merge them; pull request, merge commits only, the bazel/worker/version checks, signed commits and no deletion or force push stay; no approval is required, since the owner cannot approve the release pull request scripts/release.sh opens as them. GitHub cannot narrow a role bypass to one person, so the other admin can still update prod (docs/prod.md says so). Evidence: bash scripts/test-setup-prod-github.sh passes, including 'only the bypass actors update prod, and no approval is required', which failed before the rule was added; //scripts:setup_prod_github PASSED in just test-affected main. Not yet applied to GitHub: scripts/setup-prod-github.sh --i-know-what-i-am-doing writes it.","supersedes":"891f8d683984aaadb35c989c4214cd4d614c1bc1cb847ad8cbf3f9db1fa13c4b","tags":["status:decided","reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/cloudflare-setup.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T20:08:52.815583Z","id":"b1739aba6635e0349e5de1ce44b5e9e9060af44d516b8d55642cd94cc0e950a4","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"94ed1091a425116a0ae59a2e9803b7691c46f2f8fb2476fd3bc868f9a841953e","summary":"--no-build (added in 3d0e9dcd5) was checked the same way, by hand: a copy of the script under a scratch root with stub pnpm-install-stamped.sh, npm-ci-stamped.sh and deploy.mjs printed 'skipped (--no-build: the packages an earlier run installed)', ran neither install stub, and passed --no-build to deploy.mjs; without it both stubs ran. Still no test in scripts/ runs the script.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/setup-prod-github.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T20:08:52.815786Z","id":"7392a055034657f5cf79e3c6c252a9b213f6b6f75fb2f1617e79d459d5a65e65","body":{"detail":"The ruleset's bypass actor is the repository admin role (actor_id 5, RepositoryRole), so with the update rule every admin, not only the owner, can merge into and push to prod. A bypass actor of actor_type Team (an empathic team whose one member is the owner) would narrow it to the owner, at the cost of a team to keep and of the admin role's bypass for the release pin push (scripts/release.sh pushes it as the owner, who would be in the team).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":172},"end":{"line":172},"content_hash":"888c0d0c5504a1004585ecb2f7e1357dc62347d16d3b56ac51316198dc4dadfa"},"summary":"Bypass prod's ruleset as a team holding only the owner, not the admin role","tags":["security","revisit:the repository gains an admin other than the owner who should not deploy, or the owner asks that only they can update prod","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/bazel-derive.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:06:10.570125Z","id":"63caa98fb0b1cc0a5920e78b29add84837933bc50cc987bc430d64b7cddb06dd","body":{"detail":"wasm_features() compares @crates_wasm's wasm32 features with `cargo tree -p clax-worker -p clax-do-vfs --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -e normal`. The build scripts' dependencies and the proc macros' own dependencies, which @crates_wasm builds for the host under the host platforms' keys, are not compared with Cargo's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":558},"end":{"line":567},"content_hash":"cb639b204bb2b1dfcce3d9cb648e1d5f4ebaab555e5971af90a7e982630dfc70"},"summary":"The wasm32 feature check compares normal dependencies only","tags":["session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:06:37.923629Z","id":"d1df436871842e914d87fe8c9a878abf77b7a24820feffe1673ea6261969ae9e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"19ed076eac262bec12a035436c05705e62de550b5728608bfe916336fa552b44","summary":"Still so under Bazel: crates/clax-worker/BUILD.bazel has targets for test-wasm.mjs, test-sandbox.mjs, test-bot.mjs, test-deploy-config.mjs, e2e.mjs and e2e-hosted.mjs, and none for test-repos.mjs.","tags":["session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/npm-ci-stamped.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T01:37:42.270245Z","id":"6536251417b03515aca065420416ce00ce96301838bbede27af41f34613dcab6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4ac619dde","summary":"Taken in 4ac619dde: crates/clax-worker installs with pnpm from crates/clax-worker/pnpm-lock.yaml (the same 91 packages), through scripts/pnpm-install-stamped.sh in scripts/cloudflare-setup.sh, scripts/quality_gates.sh and scripts/worker-checks.sh, and under Bazel through rules_js (npm_worker in MODULE.bazel); scripts/npm-ci-stamped.sh is deleted. `bazelisk test //crates/clax-worker:deploy_lib_test //crates/clax-worker:deploy_config_test //scripts/...` passed (31 of 31) on this branch after its rebase onto cf4b45cd6, and PR #33's CI bazel job passed the Worker's wrangler and browser tests on Linux.","supersedes":"1bbd149ecbccd48cd976630f7121239641fe9b92fd8daef0106c6198c35cba74","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/run.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:36:07.215145Z","id":"1968a917273ffb29bb86bc2a6dff1b88d2a534af03885c492a87daf0f904ba74","body":{"detail":"The native branch (scripts/run.sh:294-297) passes the arguments to `cargo test ... -- --ignored \"$@\"`, so a word is a test-name filter; the Bazel branch appends them after //crates/clax-fleet:postgres, where `just fleet-pg-test fencing` is read as a target and fails. The justfile comment (justfile:41) does not say which.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":206},"end":{"line":210},"content_hash":"8890d9c6bf15a30444dbe1726ffb6fec429f9453356d1aa507eb6b12b8049bfc"},"suggested_fix":"Under Bazel turn bare words into `--test_arg=<word>` (or `--test_filter`), keeping flags that start with `--` as Bazel flags, and say in the justfile comment that the arguments filter tests.","summary":"`just fleet-pg-test <name>` means a test filter natively but a Bazel target pattern under Bazel","tags":["review","review:k8s-deep","devops","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/run.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:41:21.164149Z","id":"970c8891614fcb3ebf48719262aba8a2c8302aca05ab57a6dd9b1788987a8ee9","body":{"detail":"scripts/run.sh:206-210 (Bazel) appends \"$@\" after //crates/clax-fleet:postgres, so a bare word is read as a target pattern; scripts/run.sh:294-297 (native) runs cargo test -p clax-fleet --test postgres -- --ignored \"$@\", where it is a test-name filter. justfile:40-42 does not say which.","kind":"comment","references":"1968a917273ffb29bb86bc2a6dff1b88d2a534af03885c492a87daf0f904ba74","summary":"confirmed: fleet-pg-test arguments are a test filter natively and Bazel arguments under Bazel","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/run.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:00:22.764999Z","id":"22bfe80145ea33413c2d1e715dfd34850be4227bd03837f3a9e16193a8264861","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:347050368","summary":"scripts/run.sh turns bare words into --test_arg under Bazel; `CLAX_TEST_PG_URL=... ./scripts/run.sh --dry-run fleet-pg-test fencing --config=x` printed `... --test_arg=--ignored --test_arg=fencing --config=x //crates/clax-fleet:postgres`; the justfile comment says a word filters.","supersedes":"1968a917273ffb29bb86bc2a6dff1b88d2a534af03885c492a87daf0f904ba74","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/affected-tests.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T04:11:54.891787Z","id":"5035c14821c34845d1e0335b8c43c8342a2ed4a17625d7aaae0df5a798bd3383","body":{"detail":"On 2026-10-29, at main f7e862ab0 plus a branch changing crates/clax-http, crates/clax-server, web/quickstart and docs (9 files), just test-affected stopped with: ERROR: Evaluation of subquery \"deps(//...)\" failed: preloading transitive closure failed: no such target '@@rules_android_ndk++android_ndk_repository_extension+androidndk//toolchains/llvm/prebuilt/linux-x86_64:bin/clang': Label ... crosses boundary of subpackage '@@rules_android_ndk++android_ndk_repository_extension+androidndk//'; error: bazel query failed (exit 7). The same recipe ran on this machine before the Worker's Bazel build (f7e862ab0) landed, which compiles ring's and SQLite's C for wasm32 with the NDK's clang. Any change set with a file the query looks up (the deps(//...) branch at line 258) reaches it; the rdeps-only branch (line 261) does not. Running the touched packages' tests directly (bazelisk test //crates/clax-server/... etc.) works meanwhile.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":258},"end":{"line":274},"content_hash":"e210b29ee2419d61facc34ca74863a5d2416ee60fef9895f1bc575a3cb5793a0"},"summary":"just test-affected fails before testing anything: its deps(//...) query fails on the Android NDK repository's labels","tags":["ci","bazel","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/reel-stream.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T17:13:46.717037Z","id":"8779e37675eefb65d7e4285c23f14f4b3110c0af5246040535cb50188d0a1294","body":{"detail":"It is the same frame only because web/reel/compose/landing.sh opens the teaser on the shot it names as --poster (globe@touch+1.1). A cut whose teaser starts elsewhere shows a different poster on clax.dev than under clax-dev-local, which serves reel-poster.jpg. Uploading reel-poster.jpg (to the ASSETS bucket, say) or setting the video's thumbnailTimestampPct from cut.json would remove the coupling.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":113},"end":{"line":121},"content_hash":"c021a6584dc73fcd10d5404fdd9a66959b968066f6ae79227bb0aac9fce07064"},"summary":"The landing page's poster on clax.dev is Stream's default thumbnail, the reel's first frame, not reel-poster.jpg","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/crate-package.py","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:06:45.501915Z","id":"6baf73c724cc6330ec66e28aad9010de0fdcd46fef85d98af4a804a7c12370d1","body":{"detail":"LICENSE:82-85 says a package's own metadata names the same licenses as LICENSE's list. The generated clax crate embeds web/dist, whose bridge.js and overlay.js are built from web/bridge and web/overlay, which LICENSE:65-71 now puts under LGPL-2.1-only; scripts/crate-package.py:38-40 explains the expression as 'the web UI it embeds is AGPL-3.0'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":64},"end":{"line":64},"content_hash":"f248204e1939058dded4d2ab037ce476e95afb9d1e6aa3f84a65b447a4be1457"},"suggested_fix":"Make the expression `GPL-2.0-only AND AGPL-3.0-only AND LGPL-2.1-only` and update the explanation at scripts/crate-package.py:38-40.","summary":"The crates.io package's license is still GPL-2.0-only AND AGPL-3.0-only, though the web UI it embeds now includes LGPL-2.1-only bridge code","tags":["review","review:pr35-sdk-package","licensing","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/crate-package.py","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:11:00.339935Z","id":"847c7a408427fc5344079e934fb2e72bfa48f51339b521d9aeca882d8aa1412e","body":{"detail":"scripts/crate-package.py:64 \"license\": \"GPL-2.0-only AND AGPL-3.0-only\"; :38-40 explains it as 'the web UI it embeds is AGPL-3.0'; :308-331 copy web/dist into the package. web/vite.bridge.config.ts:18-19 builds bridge/src/bridge.ts to dist/_clax/bridge.js and web/vite.overlay.config.ts:15-16 builds overlay/src/main.ts to dist/_clax/overlay.js; LICENSE:65-71 now puts web/bridge, web/overlay and web/sdk under LGPL-2.1-only, and LICENSE:82-85 requires package metadata to name the same licenses. Line citations correct.","kind":"comment","references":"6baf73c724cc6330ec66e28aad9010de0fdcd46fef85d98af4a804a7c12370d1","summary":"confirmed: crate license omits LGPL-2.1-only though the embedded web/dist carries bridge.js and overlay.js built from LGPL code","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/release.sh","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T23:26:06.223220Z","id":"385aa094fb057db117bd24e1075687d722d2ea98ff58e5ffb82d69a6ac73aec8","body":{"detail":"scripts/release.sh publishes @empathic/clax-sdk in a step of its own after the Pi package's (step 21, publish-sdk.yml, or a first version from this machine), so the last step is now 22 (LAST=22). Two consequences to confirm: (1) learn_weights reads only logs whose lines say 'of 22' (the existing rule for a renumbering, scripts/release.sh:199-201), so the durations learned from earlier releases' logs under target/release/ are dropped and the next estimate uses typical durations, with 180s for the SDK publish; (2) docs and messages that named step 21 as 'What is left' now name step 22 (docs/usage.md, 'Releasing'). The other choice was one step 20 publishing both packages, which keeps the numbering but mixes two packages' resume and first-publish states in one step. The first SDK publish also installs web/'s dependencies with pnpm in a temporary worktree under target/release/ (sdk_publish_from), as the first Pi publish does for plugins/pi (waiver b354b3cf on scripts/release.sh).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":69},"end":{"line":77},"content_hash":"05059f1ce33f0334f17dcb6f00c6080bf7be34d2f1a0312153adf6510caaaa68"},"suggested_fix":"Keep step 21 for the SDK and 22 for what is left, or fold both publishes into step 20; either way say whether the first SDK publish may install web/'s dependencies as the Pi's does.","summary":"The SDK package's publish is a new step 21, which renumbers 'What is left' from 21 to 22","tags":["status:needs-decision","npm","release","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/crate-package.py","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T23:36:12.417783Z","id":"5cf8cb391d1fe39c013629aac1787e4a050b59c94c4b7b599fb2fb644f502604","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3b06dda8","summary":"PACKAGE's license is now 'GPL-2.0-only AND AGPL-3.0-only AND LGPL-2.1-only' and the docstring (scripts/crate-package.py:38-42) and docs/usage.md ('The crates.io package') say the embedded bridge and overlay scripts are built from the LGPL-2.1 web/bridge and web/overlay. ./scripts/crate-package.py printed 'wrote target/crate-package/clax (clax 0.6.0, commit 3b06dda88a3a)' and the generated Cargo.toml line 6 reads license = \"GPL-2.0-only AND AGPL-3.0-only AND LGPL-2.1-only\". Nothing else reads the expression (grep over scripts/ and docs/).","supersedes":"6baf73c724cc6330ec66e28aad9010de0fdcd46fef85d98af4a804a7c12370d1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/crate-package.py","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T23:36:40.291217Z","id":"d34e3c9b20e647b5bdf0a5bf9f9af183c62d8c3e62656d3ba041f4d7a5a88f47","body":{"detail":"Not taken: it makes about eleven internal crates (clax-core, clax-store, clax-server, ...) public crates.io names that others can depend on, each release has to publish them in layer order with versioned path dependencies, and clax-embedded would still need its web UI, extension and plugins copied inside its own directory at publish time. The generated package keeps every internal crate private at the cost of rewriting paths (rewrite_sources, lines 242-265).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2},"end":{"line":45},"content_hash":"182c369212f863faee35dc8a68746505040bd1e33434bf28c3044679c28ec4c8"},"summary":"Publish every workspace crate to crates.io instead of one generated clax package","supersedes":"b53bd589bacd49c96f643e1d4879e9852fb60d71516b966a1f6fa5a1213a01f6","tags":["revisit:a workspace crate is wanted as a library on crates.io, or the path rewrite in scripts/crate-package.py breaks on a source pattern it cannot handle","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/crate-package.py","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T23:36:40.388307Z","id":"005f28bb33700ccb0f3ee5af7cd3289f1d17d0d514d4dbc154ab1a32ee753af6","body":{"detail":"rewrite_sources replaces every crate:: in a bundled library crate's sources with crate::<module>:: and every clax_<name>:: with crate::clax_<name>::, comments and string literals included. True of the sources at this commit (git grep finds none of these patterns in the eleven bundled crates' src/). A #[macro_export] macro would move to the package root and break its crate::<module>:: callers; a crate feature would be dropped (merged_dependencies refuses optional dependencies); a string such as a serde 'with = \"crate::x\"' is rewritten, which is right, but a log or error message quoting a path would change. tracing targets already read clax::clax_server::... in the package instead of clax_server::... . just crate-package (cargo check --locked of the packed crate) catches whatever does not compile.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":242},"end":{"line":265},"content_hash":"60a7470fdeceb23fa40696d9dd071b492298c652ad77d652836201163f9e7bbe"},"summary":"The package's module rewrite is textual and assumes the bundled crates have no #[macro_export] macros, no extern crate, no crate features and no strings naming crate paths","supersedes":"da1375a6e1d55495ecc3365a25b08d53908df9c9261f0f995162cde93fd8b949","tags":["session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/crate-package.py","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T23:36:55.518180Z","id":"3ba17507187869a41ac25e1bde14de50f0075b1b45a23dc4c2e7e2c239a119e4","body":{"detail":"merged_dependencies (scripts/crate-package.py:121-140) no longer refuses an optional dependency: it leaves it out, dropped_features (lines 98-118) names every feature that turns one on, and rewrite_sources (line 469-470) replaces each such feature = \"<name>\" in the bundled sources with any(). The concern's 'no crate features' and 'merged_dependencies refuses optional dependencies' now hold only for features that turn on no optional dependency, which are still dropped silently; the rest of the concern (crate:: rewrite in comments and strings, #[macro_export], extern crate) stands. The owner may revise the root's summary.","kind":"comment","references":"005f28bb33700ccb0f3ee5af7cd3289f1d17d0d514d4dbc154ab1a32ee753af6","span":{"start":{"line":242},"end":{"line":265},"content_hash":"60a7470fdeceb23fa40696d9dd071b492298c652ad77d652836201163f9e7bbe"},"summary":"Since this branch the rewrite handles one kind of crate feature: an optional dependency's features are dropped and read as any()","supersedes":"e2118ee1f88ca176f1fd003354a46efc38537330c3026bb43e12dac1112b7b72","tags":["session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/crate-package.py","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T16:20:15.725799Z","id":"673bc4c28670629e242c762595397285d5ffd8663ed0fca3fdd62849ddbe8718","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3af33a0bc97db3e90a7a41823d86c72fbb8a2c81","summary":"PACKAGE's license is now 'GPL-2.0-only AND AGPL-3.0-only AND LGPL-2.1-only' and the docstring (scripts/crate-package.py:38-42) and docs/usage.md ('The crates.io package') say the embedded bridge and overlay scripts are built from the LGPL-2.1 web/bridge and web/overlay. ./scripts/crate-package.py printed 'wrote target/crate-package/clax (clax 0.6.0, commit 3af33a0b8a3a)' and the generated Cargo.toml line 6 reads license = \"GPL-2.0-only AND AGPL-3.0-only AND LGPL-2.1-only\". Nothing else reads the expression (grep over scripts/ and docs/).","supersedes":"5cf8cb391d1fe39c013629aac1787e4a050b59c94c4b7b599fb2fb644f502604","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
